\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Opens Stronger At New 12-Year High Vs Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 536 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2011\par 14:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Brazil's real gives up some ground after breaking BRL1.53 in early trades.\par \par \uc2 --Debt-related risks in developed markets have been supporting emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 --Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in exchange market.\par \par \uc2 By Paul Kiernan\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real continued its recent offensive against the dollar Tuesday, opening at the strongest level since 1999 as emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  proved resilient to the debt-related risks that have been punishing assets in Europe and the U.S.\par \par \uc2 The real was quoted in Sao Paulo trading at BRL1.5319 to the dollar, according to Tullet Prebon via FactSet, compared with BRL1.5299 in earlier trades and BRL1.5408 at Monday's close.\par \par \uc2 Helping to fuel the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rally, some market participants say, is the ongoing stalemate among U.S. politicians in talks to raise the country's borrowing limit. As the U.S. grinds closer to an unprecedented default on its sovereign debt -- something that could happen as soon as Aug. 2 -- one view is that emerging-market countries with comparatively strong fiscal and macroeconomic fundamentals are being treated as safe havens.\par \par \uc2 But few, if any, investors know what would ultimately happen if the U.S. failed to make good on its financial obligations, with a powerful shock to the global financial system among the possibilities not to be discarded.\par \par \uc2 Win Thin, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in New York, characterized the recent appreciation of the real and other emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as "surprising."\par \par \uc2 "Maybe the market is being too complacent, but the general feeling is that, even if it comes down to an eleventh-hour thing, the U.S. is not going to default," Thin said.\par \par \uc2 He said Brazilian authorities can be expected to roll out new "roadblocks" to the real's gains, as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength is reducing the competitiveness of local manufacturers and exporters. At some point, the appreciation can be expected to slow.\par \par \uc2 "But every time the real weakens, it's seen as a buying opportunity," Thin said, adding that foreign investment money appears set to continue flowing into Brazil and supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Guido Mantega on Monday said local authorities reserve their right to implement further measures to limit the real's gains.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday was preparing a round of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market. The bank held an auction Tuesday morning to buy dollars for forward delivery on Aug. 2, the deadline set by the U.S. government for raising its debt ceiling. According to the results of the auction, the bank purchased dollars at BRL1.5340.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said it will poll market participants to gauge interest in a possible so-called reverse swap to be held Wednesday. Reverse swap auctions allow investors to exchange volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 -linked contracts for paper indexed to domestic rates, and have been used by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reduce the volume of dollar-linked paper in the local market.\par \par \uc2 -By Paul Kiernan, Dow Jones Newswires; (+55)11-3544-7074, paul.kiernan@dowjones.com [ 26-07-11 1341GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110726e77q00141\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
