\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Seeks To Reduce Banks'  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Short Positions\b0\par\par\uc2 492 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2011\par 13:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Update with \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 's comments in the 6th and 7th paragraphs)\par \par \uc2 By Rogerio Jelmayer\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sought to reduce dollar short positions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to slow \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows into Brazil, at least in the short-term.\par \par \uc2 Banks will now have to deposit 60% of the value of their positions above $1 billion without any remuneration, and have just five days to adjust respective positions, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 In January, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced a similar measure. Then, however, banks had more time to adjust. At the time, banks had to deposit 60% of the value of their positions above $3 billion without any remuneration, and had 90 days to adjust their positions.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian banks had a net $14.7 billion in bets against the dollar at the end of June, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bets against the dollar are a constant source of upward pressure on the Brazilian real, which worries the government because of the impact of a stronger real on exporters, particularly manufacturers. With a stronger real, Brazilian goods become more expensive in terms of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Clearly, the recent bout of BRL appreciation has generated some discomfort in the government. We believe the measures should force banks that are not in compliance with the new limits to increase demand for spot USD (US Dollar) and also increase the supply of short USD in the futures markets, hence affecting the on-off short basis as well," \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  said in a research report for its clients.\par \par \uc2 "The BCB's (Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) first move on spot short USD positions was last January (announcing the $3 billion threshold) and by tightening the limits again, this means that authorities know some institutions will have to move to the market to square their positions. Even though we do not have individual information, the system carries $14.7 billion in short spot USD positions. And we believe the BCB is aiming to drive this stock to closer to $10 billion," \uc2 Barclays\uc2  added.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the Brazilian real finished active trading at BRL1.5627 to the dollar, weaker against Thursday's close of BRL1.5556, according to Tullet Prebon via Factset.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday stepped up its market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in an apparent attempt to "take advantage" of risk aversion to roll back some of the real's recent gains.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian officials have been keen to stall, or even reverse, the real's appreciation against the dollar. The real has gained 20% against the dollar over the past two years.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market three times Friday, twice with snap auctions to buy dollars and once with a reverse swap auction.\par \par \uc2 -By Rogerio Jelmayer, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511-3544-7071; rogerio.jelmayer@dowjones.com [ 11-07-11 1155GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110711e77b000wg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
