\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real, Mexico peso mark 2008 highs\b0\par\par\uc2 694 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 2011\par 17:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil resigned to more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains - for now\par \par \uc2 * U.S. jobs data supports bids for region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Brazil real firms 1.16 pct, Mexico peso up 0.41 pct\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle and Jean Luis Arce\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, April 1 (Reuters) - Brazil's real and Mexico's peso hit their strongest levels in more than 2 years on Friday, but further gains ahead may be limited by increased \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  and heavy positioning in the peso.\par \par \uc2 Investors were expecting tough new measures from Brazil this week, but a tax on foreign debt held by locals fell far short of expectations, and investors bet policymakers had lost their nerve to impose severe capital controls.\par \par \uc2 The real surged this week by nearly 3 percent in its biggest weekly gain in a year week as investors tested the resolve of authorities to contain \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength that is hurting local manufacturers.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian officials confirmed to Reuters they were unwilling to impose -- at least for now -- more severe capital controls to weaken one of the world's most overvalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nN01172691]\par \par \uc2 After trying a range of measures to contain gains in the real, policymakers are left with drastic capital control options that could spur sharp losses - and further inflame inflation by making imports more expensive.\par \par \uc2 "The government's increased concerns about inflation and its effects on the population's real income are probably driving this increased tolerance for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength," said Nick Chamie, head of emerging market research at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  in Toronto.\par \par \uc2 The real <BRBY> bid 1.16 percent firmer at 1.61 per dollar on the local spot market, its strongest levels since August 2008.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  blew past the 1.65 per dollar level that was considered authorities unofficial limit, and now the market expects the next line in the sand to be drawn around 1.60 per dollar level.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian authorities have been trying to block unwanted flows attracted to the country's double-digit interest rates, but investors continue to find ways around each new barrier.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did its best to contain the real's gains, holding three auctions in the spot market, in a marked increase in of its efforts. Increased \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely contain further gains next week, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Supporting demand for riskier emerging market assets, U.S. employment recorded a second straight month of solid gains in March. [ID:nNOAT00477]\par \par \uc2 The gains were seen as solid enough to keep up confidence in the U.S. recovery, but not strong enough to discourage the Federal Reserve from its ultra-easy monetary policies that has boosted the appeal of higher yielding Latin American debt.\par \par \uc2 "This is helping risk appetite, and should carry emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stronger as economic prospects improve," Chamie said.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=> gained 0.41 percent to 11.84 per dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  touched its strongest level since October 2008 and gained around 1 percent this week.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has benefited from signs of an improving economic recovery in the United States, its top trading partner, as well as expectations that Mexican authorities will not increase their current pace of building dollar reserves.\par \par \uc2 However, so many people are betting on a stronger peso, that the lack of important U.S. economic data next week to back up optimism could leave the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  open to profit taking.\par \par \uc2 Data showed a net $3.7 billion in speculative futures contracts betting on a stronger peso, the highest number of speculative contracts of the eight major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracked by Reuters. [ID:nN01141556]\par \par \uc2 "If we get a negative shock, (the peso) will turn around in a second," said Roberto Melzi, a strategist at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso hit a three-week high, boosted by market expectations of another 50 basis-point interest rate increase in April following publication of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  minutes from the March rate-setting meeting. [ID:nN01110945]\par \par \uc2 The peso <CLP=CL> bid 0.42 percent stronger at 475.5 per dollar, for an around 0.7 percent advance for the week.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110404e7410016d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
