\par\par \uc2 Top Stories\par \b \uc2 Brazil Says No Offers Accepted In Reverse Auction\b0\par\par\uc2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 17:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Top News & Commentary\par \uc2 DJCOMM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took a new twist Thursday, as it rejected all offers in a reverse swap auction, in what some market players see as a battle of wills with local banks.\par \par \uc2 No contracts were sold in a first reverse swap auction, and a second reverse swap auction was immediately called to end at 1600 GMT.\par \par \uc2 This is the first time that no bids were accepted since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  restarted the reverse swap auctions earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 "What we've had since Tuesday is the treasury departments at the banks are testing the firepower of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  with heavy selling orders," said Luiz Carlos Baldan, a director at FourTrade Corretora de Cambio in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 The market's perception is that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to weaken the real to BRL1.67 in the short term, and BRL1.70 to BRL1.80 by year-end, to help exporters, he said.\par \par \uc2 "Banks on the other hand want to see ... what measures the government can take," Baldan said. "There's no short-term gain for the banks, but it gives them an idea of how much power they have to manipulate exchange rates."\par \par \uc2 The real gained sharply at the open on Thursday, but weakened after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . As well as the reverse swap auction, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held two auctions to buy dollars in the spot market.\par \par \uc2 At 1519 GMT, the real was trading at BRL1.6253, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. That was stronger than Wednesday's closing of BRL1.6275.\par \par \uc2 The terms on offer in the second auction were identical to the first: three lots of up to 10,000 contracts, valued at the equivalent of $1.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 -By Matthew Cowley, Dow Jones Newswires; +55 11 3544 7082; matthew.cowley@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 --Rogerio Jelmayer contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCOMM1120110331e73v000tq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
