\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Fights On All Fronts, But Real Still Shines\b0\par\par\uc2 889 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 20:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  faces a credibility problem as inflation expectations deteriorate\par \par \uc2 -The real has outperformed despite new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures\par \par \uc2 -Carry trades remain attractive as some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves have removed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Erin McCarthy \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's ongoing efforts to curb its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's appreciation have removed volatility from the Brazilian real, but that could mean that's backfiring.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Less volatility, some investors say, only makes the Brazilian real more attractive for carry trades. In such trades, investors borrow money in a low-yielding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the dollar and reinvest the proceeds in short-term securities in a high-yielding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the real. Such trades can be highly profitable but risky because sharp, unexpected turns can impose big losses on leveraged positions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That leaves the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a tight bind and is raising concern it is falling behind the inflation curve. Prices continue to rise in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , despite its towering interest rates. Yet, its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  haven't spooked international investors away from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with the real breaking through the bank's unofficial line in the sand this week. That makes Brazilian exports less competitive and leaves the country's financial system vulnerable if at some time in the future the inflows in yield-seeking "hot money" turn into rapid outflows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indeed, the real stayed significantly stronger than BRL1.65 to the dollar on Thursday, just days after the bank announced its newest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  efforts, a 6% tax on foreign bond issuance to help stem repatriation flows that drive real-buying.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The bank's methods, which include such macroprudential measures as taxes on certain types of investments, have slowed the pace of inflows and the real's appreciation, analysts say. The bank also regularly buys dollars in the spot, forward and futures markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But these moves have actually taken volatility out of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which only further entices carry-trade investors into Brazilian money markets, where interest rates are among the highest in the world. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Selic base rate is at 11.75%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We like [the] Brazilian real even with the macroprudential tools that have been put in place," said Michael Mata, who manages the ING \f28 \uc2 \f2 Global Bond Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "We don't think it's going to appreciate dramatically from here, but it doesn't need to with a 12% carry."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The bank's moves have also reduced "speculative elements," helping to further diminish volatility, said Adnan Akant, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and managing director at money manager \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fischer Francis Trees & Watts\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a New York unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What's more, with Brazil being such a costly market to enter, and with such a stable \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  making carry-trades a relatively safe bet, few investors are willing to leave the real, even in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's wake. "It's one of those buy-and-hold \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Akant said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Such views are giving the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  a headache.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real's relentless popularity is evident in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's most recent published weekly figures for money flows. Although they showed some money slipped away from Brazil over the last week, net dollar receipts still stood at $10.52 billion in March through last Friday, up from only $462 million in the same period of last year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Corporate flows have been a primary source of the real's strength, while hot money flows represent only a portion, said RBS strategist Flavia Cattan-Naslausky. In addition, excess global liquidity has driven investors to emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  like the real.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The flipside of this, however, is that the combination of macroprudential and more orthodox \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  measures have created a growing credibility problem for the bank, as inflation expectations continue to deteriorate.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , in its quarterly report out Wednesday, raised its 2011 inflation forecast to 5.6% from 5.0%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  efforts up-to-date have been deemed ineffective.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We don't really think any of this is really going to have an impact [on the real]," said Tony Volpon, head of Americas emerging-market research at Nomura.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, by allowing the real to go stronger than BRL1.65, the bank may be signaling a small shift in its line in the sand, though it will likely defend new levels, analysts said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In coming weeks, the bank could focus on more orthodox measures in the spot and futures markets, Cattan-Naslausky said. It may allow more volatility through sporadic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , ending the real's predictability, which could squeeze out some of the stale positions in dollar-Brazil and help it weaken, she added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The next few days will be crucial in telling where the bank plans to head, as markets wait to see how far the bank will let the real go, analysts said. In the mean time, investors will likely stay in the real unless more volatility surfaces or if global events damp risk sentiment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "As long as you have confidence that at some future date everything is going to be okay in Brazil, then you're okay," Akant said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Erin McCarthy, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Matthew Cowley and Gerald Jeffris contributed to this article. [ 03-31-11 1445ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110331e73v000at\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
