\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Weakens In Late Trade After  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Acts\b0\par\par\uc2 563 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 22:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real weakened marginally in late trading Thursday, after heavy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  limited the U.S. dollar's fall amid continued speculative trading in the run-up to the setting of the end-of-month Ptax \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate used to settle futures contracts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The real traded at BRL1.6305 at 2000 GMT, weaker than its Wednesday close of BRL1.6275, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset.\par \par \uc2 Investors, including Brazilian banks, were reported to have driven down the dollar rate against the real for the fourth consecutive day in a move to gain on futures and reverse swap maturities. Traders noted that Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to wait until these "technical" market movements subside before resuming its strategy to curb the real's trend to appreciation.\par \par \uc2 However, economists said new measures could now be adopted anytime as more market stability should be seen following the settling of the Ptax rate later Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "We believe that the market may return to normal levels [Friday], with a higher, more civilized rate for the dollar, maybe of around BRL1.65 to BRL1.66," said Luiz Antonio Abdo of \uc2 Corretora Souza Barros\uc2 . "The downwards movement we've been seeing on the dollar since the start of the week is because of the tug of war between banks and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the Ptax rate."\par \par \uc2 A new increased tax on foreign loans announced earlier this week was seen to be having little immediate impact on market exchange rates. Traders said large quantities of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continue to enter Brazil as Brazilian companies including banks continue to seek financing in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The spot dollar, which lost 1.39% against the real amid Wednesday's speculative movements, opened trading Thursday at its lowest level since August 27, 2008, at the start of the subprime crisis. However, massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which bought up dollars at three spot auctions and organized two reverse-swap auctions, propped up the dollar to the extent that it showed small gains towards the end of the trading day.\par \par \uc2 "The true face of the exchange market will, however, be apparent only next week," said Raphael Martello of Tendencias Consultoria.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first reverse-swap auction, at which 30,000 contracts were offered at auction, found no takers, demonstrating Brazilian banks' unwillingness to participate in this kind of trade, which doesn't bring them any specific benefit, Martello said. "The banks think they won't make any gain from this instrument, as they believe the real's going to appreciate further," the economist observed. "The banks prefer not to take the risk."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's second reverse-swap auction in early afternoon sold just 22% of the lots on offer.\par \par \uc2 Reverse-swap contracts offer investors the opportunity to exchange dollar-linked futures contracts for paper linked to interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The government has been using reverse-swap auctions, along with other mechanisms, in recent months in order to arrest the appreciation of the real. The strong real hurts Brazilian exporters and manufacturers.\par \par \uc2 The real has gained 45% against the dollar over the past two years.\par \par \uc2 -By Diana Kinch, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-21-2586-6086; diana.kinch@dowjones.com [ 31-03-11 2046GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110331e73v001io\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
