\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Aggressive In  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Trade\b0\par\par\uc2 150 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 17:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 11:03 (Dow Jones) After tepid, routine \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the week, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  turns aggressive in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. In morning trading, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys dollars at a snap auction and then calls an auction of reverse swap contracts that could sweep up as much as $1.5B in future dollar deliveries. More \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could follow in the afternoon. The bank is sweating to arrest further unwanted appreciation of the Brazilian real, which gained sharply against the American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday. In late morning trading, the real is again stronger against the dollar at BRL1.6244 versus BRL1.6275 at the close Wednesday. (tom.murphy@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2184 or email paul.vigna@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\uc2  [ 03-31-11 1103ET ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843 80000   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020110331e73v000cq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
