\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Intervention \highlight\uc2  Not Seen As Forceful\b0\par\par\uc2 1,289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 19:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1:42 (Dow Jones) \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move to call a snap reverse auction is an attempt to weaken the real, says \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  strategist Win Thin. Still, he says he is surprised policymakers "haven't been more forceful. It's nothing new in their arsenal, which people were waiting for." Real sharply stronger against dollar today with USD/BRL down 1% to 1.6320. (anjali.cordeiro@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-3100 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 1:26 (Dow Jones) US rate futures prices back off day's highs after $29B 7-year Treasury note auction is considered a little bit weak. Jun 10-year Tsy note futures pull back a bit from 119-07 session high. Recently 9+/32 higher at 119-02. Quarterly 2012 Eurodollar futures recently as much as 5.5 BP higher, having been up as much as 7.5 BP at the pre-auction high. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-3100 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 1535 GMT [Dow Jones] Portugal's five-year sovereign CDS are at 566 bps, which would represent its highest ever closing level, although it is possible that higher intraday prices were seen in January, Markit says. 5-year protection prices appear to have been volatile, rising to 555 bps early before dropping down to 548 bps mid-morning, 2 bps tighter from Tuesday. Fitch says Wednesday that Portugal needs financial support and a "timely and credible" economic program from the European Union and the International Monetary Fund to avoid a likely downgrade. (mark.brown@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1511 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 HSBC\uc2  says to sell the zloty ahead of Poland's revised 4Q current account release due Thursday. The bank warns the imports data may be substantially upwardly revised and this could be very negative for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "A possible revision of the huge 'errors & omissions' constitutes a threat to the PLN, particularly in a context of high fiscal deficit," \uc2 HSBC\uc2  says, adds the emergence of a 'twin deficit' would have a lasting negative impact on the PLN. "In our view only a more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action would offer PLN protection," \uc2 HSBC\uc2  says.(malgorzata.halaba@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1506 GMT [Dow Jones] June gilts are ending Wednesday off their lows, but are still down 0.40 at 117.31 on the day, after what one strategist calls an "uneventful" day with moves "mostly flow driven." Adds that the market has been inclined to sell off as the relative stability in peripheral euro-zone sovereign bonds Wednesday means there is no flight-to-safety bid. Thursday brings Nationwide and Hometrack UK housing data. 10-year gilts yield 3.67%, up from 3.62% Tuesday. (mark.brown@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1448 GMT [Dow Jones] Hungarian government bonds strengthen mainly in the long end of the curve by around 15bp due to high interest in the series 2019/A bond at Wednesday morning's exchange auction. The 3-year benchmark bond yield is 6.72%-6.62%, 5-year is 6.98%-6.88%, 10-year is 7.22%-7.12%. Bonds could weaken over the coming days, as signaled by low trading volumes and a decreasing number of buyers on the scene, one trader says. Yields could weaken by around 15-20bp from current levels until the end of this week. (veronika.gulyas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:29 (Dow Jones) Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  indicated rate hikes are likely coming to an end in its quarterly inflation report out today, says BES Investimentos. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inflation forecasts point to lower inflation in 2011 and 2012, despite the current upward trend, so "we believe the tightening cycle is getting close to an end," it says. "Therefore, we stick to our call the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase benchmark rates by 50bps in April, which should be the last movement on basic interest rates." (matthew.cowley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-3100 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 1415 GMT [Dow Jones] Export-driven Hungary is expected to have generated a current account surplus of EUR180 million in 4Q 2010 due to its steadily strong trade surplus, 7 economists polled by Dow Jones Newswires say. The 3Q surplus was EUR476.7 million. Forecasts came in a wide range: between a deficit of EUR800 million and a surplus of EUR255 million, reflecting uncertainties surrounding profit repatriations by foreign companies operating in Hungary. 2010 current account surplus is forecast at EUR1.8 billion, a swing from a 2009 deficit of EUR119.8 million. Hungary hasn't generated an annual surplus for the past 15 years, or for as long as data go back on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's website. Figures are due at 0630 GMT Thursday. (margit.feher@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1351 GMT [Dow Jones] Polish bonds are almost flat ahead of rate decision next week, traders say. Also, the market awaits details of debt supply for April to be issued Thursday or Friday. Average yields on 2 and 5-year bonds are unchanged from late Tuesday, at 5.01% and 5.78%, respectively. Average yield on 10-year paper is at 6.28% from 6.29%. (malgorzata.halaba@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1348 GMT [Dow Jones] A lackluster, risk-neutral day in the bund market, with low volumes and a very narrow trading range. The June contract, currently down 0.18 at 121.32, has been stuck in a 121.16-121.40 band with investors now looking ahead to the outcome of Thursday's Irish bank stress tests and Friday's U.S. non-farm payrolls reading. In the cash space, the 2s/5s/10s yield 1.758%/2.652%/3.343% with cross-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spreads against gilts widening by 1-3 bps and remaining unchanged against US Treasurys. In the core markets, Italy's successful EUR9B multi-tranche auction caused bund/BTP spreads to tighten by 1.5-3.5 bps over the 2/10-year curve. (nick.cawley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:10 (Dow Jones) New ADP data may be better than it seems at first blush. Report points to an increasingly optimistic take on the US jobs market, and by extension USD, says Alan Ruskin of \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 . "The 3-month average of ADP has been above 200K for 2 months which is a comparatively rare event," says Ruksin. "This 'feat' was achieved only once in the prior recovery back in 2004." EUR/USD off slightly in Wed global session, recently trading at 1.4093 from 1.4113 late Tuesday, according to EBS via CQG. (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-3100 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 8:29 (Dow Jones) EUR/USD inches up to 1.4099 from 1.4089 after weaker-than-expected ADP jobs survey, but is still down roughly 0.10% on session. For US data this week, Friday's non-farm payrolls report remains the focus of market. ADP data have not been viewed of late as any great predictor of the government's data and so trade has been muted based on these surveys. USD/JPY largely unchanged at 83.02 from 83.04 just before data. (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-3100 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\uc2 . [ 03-30-11 1342ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110330e73u000a7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
