roup annual report. \par  \par  2.    Basis of Preparation \par        The financial information set out in this announcement \par         does not constitute the Group's statutory financial \par         statements for the years ended 31 December 2010 or 2009, \par         but is derived from those accounts. The auditors have \par         reported on those accounts and their reports were unqualified. \par         The Group closely monitors and manages its liquidity \par         risk. The Group has considerable financial resources \par         including US$130.1 million in cash and cash equivalents \par         and the Groups borrowings have a long maturity profile. \par         Based on the Group's cash forecasts and sensitivities \par         run the Directors have a reasonable expectation that \par         the Company and the Group have adequate resources to \par         continue in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  existence for the foreseeable \par         future. For this reason, they continue to adopt the \par         going concern basis in preparing the accounts. \par        Whilst the financial information included in this preliminary \par         announcement has been prepared in accordance with International \par         Financial Reporting Standards (IFRSs), this announcement \par         does not itself contain sufficient information to comply \par         with IFRSs. \par  \par  \par  3.    Revenue \par  \par                                                   Year ended    Year ended \par        An analysis of the Group's revenue \par         is as follows:                           31 December   31 December \par                                                         2010          2009 \par                                                      US$'000       US$'000 \par  \par   Sales of services                                  536,258       455,801 \par   Revenue from construction \par    contracts                     