\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Currency \highlight\uc2  Market Weaker On Possible  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Portugal\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jeff Fick   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 528 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 14:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market traded weaker Wednesday amid renewed expectations for government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and concerns about Europe's debt troubles.\par \par \uc2 Skittish investors were once again searching for safety as fiscal and debt woes in Europe jumped into the headlines. The government of Portuguese Prime Minister Jose Socrates faces a key vote on a fiscal austerity package that had been expected to keep the country from asking for a European Union bailout. The package is not expected to pass, and Socrates has pledged to resign if the proposal is rejected. That could force Portugal to seek a rescue package.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, the focus is on the possibility of additional "macroprudential" measures aimed at containing the strength of the real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reining in expanding credit. The market had expected a new package of measures shortly after the Carnival holiday earlier this month, but the earthquake and tsunami in Japan created uncertainty that caused the real to weaken.\par \par \uc2 Traders and analysts expect additional measures such as an increase to the IOF financial transactions tax, higher bank reserve requirements or the start of dollar purchases by Brazil's Sovereign Wealth Fund.\par \par \uc2 "Besides following movements abroad, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market players will receive and react to weekly \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows and expectations for government \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures," said Miriam Tavares, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  director at Sao Paulo-based AGK Corretora de Cambio. "That should keep trading in the recent range."\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real traded weaker at BRL1.6610 to the dollar shortly after the open, according to Tullet Prebon via Factset. The real closed Tuesday at BRL1.6585 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The market did find some support despite the gloomy outlook in Europe. In Japan, officials said that the troubled nuclear reactors had been reconnected to the power grid and control-room \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  were being restarted. That should allow workers to start cooling \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reduce the risk of a further meltdown of the nuclear fuel at the Fukushima Daiichi plant.\par \par \uc2 Inflation in Brazil, meanwhile, showed signs of easing in the period through mid-March. The mid-month inflation index rose 0.60% through mid-March compared with a 0.97% increase through mid-February. The widely watched rolling 12-month rate, however, was at 6.13%. That remained well above the government's 4.5% year-end target.\par \par \uc2 Low unemployment, higher disposable income and greater access to credit have sparked a surge in domestic demand that has pushed Brazil's inflation rate to just over 6%. The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has boosted local interest rates to 11.75%, by far the highest of any major economy, in an effort to contain prices.\par \par \uc2 The towering interest rates, however, have also caused a surge in foreign investment inflows as investors seeking higher rates of return flood into Brazil. In Senate testimony Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Alexandre Tombini said that the surge in foreign-investment inflows had created unsustainable credit growth in Latin America's largest economy.\par \par \uc2 -By Jeff Fick, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-21-2586-6085; Jeff.Fick@dowjones.com [ 23-03-11 1314GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110323e73n0011l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
