\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Tombini: Brazil Aims At Stability, Not Defense Of  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Rate\b0\par\par\uc2 170 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 15:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 22 Mar 2011 11:09 EDT DJ  Tombini: Brazil Aims At Stability, Not Defense Of \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Rate\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aims to assure stability in the local economy and not to defend a specific \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Alexandre Tombini said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "Our focus is financial stability," Tombini said when questioned specifically by members of the country's Senate economic affairs committee on whether the bank was implementing a strategy to weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought dollars heavily in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over recent months to stem the strengthening country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to some market analysts, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has set an informal ceiling for the real at around BRL1.65 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; (5561) 3335-0832, gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 22, 2011 11:09 ET (15:09 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110322e73m003vo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal33