\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Strengthens After Government Fails To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 14:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real opened stronger on Friday, recovering from a slide in the previous session after strong rumors of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  proved to be unfounded, and after the announcement of a cease-fire in Libya calmed markets.\par \par \uc2 The real opened at BRL1.6717 to the dollar, according to SIX \uc2 Telekurs\uc2  via Factset. That's weaker than Thursday's close of BRL1.6783.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slumped Thursday on speculation the Brazilian government would announce measures to contain appreciation of the real. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also declined on concern that Japanese investors would withdraw money from Brazil to rebuild their country after a massive earthquake and tsunami destroyed several cities.\par \par \uc2 Investors are wary of moves by the government to curb the real's gain, with traders saying Thursday they were expecting an increase in IOF taxes on foreign financial investments to be announced soon. The government raised the IOF to 6% from 2% last year in an effort to weaken the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whose jump of more than 35% since 2009 has harmed Brazilian exports' competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 "Yesterday we saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumble on strong rumors of new measures, but since nothing came of it, the market is giving back those declines," said Roberto Kropp, director of fixed-income trading at Daycoval Asset Management in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 The improving global environment also helped the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In addition to a stabilizing situation in Japan, Libya ordered an immediate ceasefire in the wake of a United Nations resolution passed Thursday. Libyan Foreign Minister Musa Kusa said Friday that the country would "respond positively" to the resolution and halt all military \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  against rebel forces.\par \par \uc2 Efforts by the Group of Seven to halt the yen's gain also may be helping the real, Kropp said. The Group of Seven moved overnight to stem "excess volatility and disorderly movements" in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets\par \par \uc2 "The Fed will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the yen, and that could calm markets as well as strengthen riskier \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 " like the real, he said.\par \par \uc2 -By Paulo Winterstein, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3544-7073; paulo.winterstein@dowjones.com [ 18-03-11 1301GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110318e73i0011t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
