\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-No quick fix for Brazil's strong real\b0\par\par\uc2 770 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 22:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 * Gov't measures, global portfolio shift stabilize real\par \par \uc2 * Further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unlikely to weaken real much\par \par \uc2 * Deep fiscal reforms key to long-term strategy\par \par \uc2 By Alonso Soto\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, March 15 (Reuters) - Brazil must learn to live with a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as foreigners keep their appetite for local assets and the government faces diminishing options for braking the real's rise without hurting the economy.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Guido Mantega may announce as early as this week new steps that could include time limits on investments and taxes on international loans after the real rose to 2-1/2 year highs on March 4.\par \par \uc2 Those potential changes have helped the real stabilize in recent weeks after it firmed nearly 39 percent in the last two years to become one of the world's most overvalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A barrage of government measures, along with some renewed appetite for assets in a recovering United States and Europe, have helped contain the real <BRBY> above the 1.65 per dollar mark -- considered the authorities' unofficial floor.\par \par \uc2 Still, analysts say there is little the government can do over the medium term to counteract upward pressure on the real stemming from Brazil's high interest rates and rapid recent growth.\par \par \uc2 <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :    \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/sux38r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/sux38r }}}\uc2 \f2 \par  FACTBOX \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  latest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       [ID:nN15240336]\par  SCENARIOS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  measures       [ID:nN14145427]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's economy grew 7.5 percent in 2010, its fastest pace in 24 years, spurring inflationary pressure that is expected to keep interest rates high and investors' dollars flowing in despite a recent lull in equities. [ID:nN14253010]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It is practically impossible to weaken the real given the size of the international market and the tools available for the government," said Armando Castelar Pinheiro, senior economics researcher at the Getulio Vargas Foundation, a think tank.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "A strong real is here to stay for some time -- Brazilians will have to get used to it."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DIMINISHING OPTIONS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite signs the economy will slow sharply this year as higher interest rates and budget cuts bite, dollar inflows reached $23 billion in the first two months of 2011, nearly matching the $24.35 billion that arrived in all of 2010.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazilian consumers are reaping the benefits of a stronger real, traveling abroad like never before and flooding into home appliance stores to buy foreign-made electronics.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength is hurting the country's manufacturers as they struggle to cope with a wave of cheaper Chinese imports. Industrial output dropped 0.3 percent in the fourth quarter of last year from the third quarter as household consumption jumped 2.5 percent.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New President Dilma Rousseff faces a delicate balance between relieving exporters' pain and keeping Brazil attractive for foreign direct investment, funds that could be deterred by any new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  measures.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil has already tripled, to 6 percent, the tax it charges foreigners when they buy local bonds, boosted dollar purchases and set limits on banks' short positions on the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 More and deeper controls could start to hit investor sentiment in the energy and mining powerhouse.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "You see an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy that has quite frankly expired in terms of anything beyond marginal impact on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . It just buys the government time," said Flavia Cattan-Naslausky, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with RBS in New York.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is increasing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's financing costs as heavily taxed investors see less incentive to buy longer term debt. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's dollar purchases -- over $8 billion in the spot market in February alone -- may also hit the bank's balance sheet on rising carry costs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "They are destroying some market sentiment," said Alberto Ramos, a senior economist with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "The government can anchor the real, but the question is, 'At what cost?'"\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Many analysts see the real staying between 1.65 and 1.70 per dollar in most of 2011, although shocks in international markets resulting from the aftermath of Japan's earthquake and Middle East unrest could add some volatility.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Over the longer term, analysts say the only way Brazil can weaken the real is through deeper reforms, such as reducing the large state role in the economy and raising its relatively low savings rate. Lower state spending would ease pressure on interest rates and reduce incentives for investors seeking to profit from the rate differential.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rousseff, who took office in January, has slashed some spending in this year's budget, but so far kept away from deeper reforms in her legislative agenda. [ID:nN02222605]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Editing by Stuart Grudgings and Padraic Cassidy and Dan Grebler)\f28 \par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ANALYSIS)  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110318e73f001nm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
