\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Mexico peso at highest since Oct 08, real sinks\b0\par\par\uc2 685 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 18:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Dollar flows help Mexican peso break past key level\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears hit \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real falls 0.73 pct, Mexico peso up 0.63 pct\par \par \uc2 * Chile peso loses 0.57 pct on copper slump\par \par \uc2 (Recasts; adds comments)\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, March 9 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso blew past a key technical level on Wednesday to notch a nearly 2-1/2 year high, suggesting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be able to make a further push higher after struggling in a range since January.\par \par \uc2 Traders said flows from long-term investors, including a big bet by a hedge fund, caught the market by surprise when many expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains during the session to be less sharp. A resulting scramble to buy pesos and cover losses exacerbated the break.\par \par \uc2 Demand for Mexico's exports is expected to be lifted by the recovery in the U.S. economy, and the peso may be on track to hit levels close to 11.80 per dollar that some analysts have been signaling.\par \par \uc2 "Long-term investors are entering Mexico," said Francisco Diez, director of emerging markets trading at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  in New York. "It looks like a lot of dollars went into Mexico today."\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso <MXN=> firmed 0.63 percent to 11.93 per dollar, its strongest since Oct. 2008. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  punched through its previous high at 11.9439 set in January that many thought would hold during the session.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lagged the gains in other emerging market economies. But some investors think it could try and catch up this year as the U.S. economy gains steam.\par \par \uc2 Local banks exercised $367 million in dollar put options with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, leaving $200 million of the $600 million the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling every month to build up its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 The options give banks the right to sell dollars to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a better peso rate than the spot market.\par \par \uc2 "The fact that $200 million were not exercised suggests the holders of those options think the peso could get even stronger," said Benito Berber, an analyst at Nomura Securities.\par \par \uc2 REAL SLUMPS\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real recoiled on fresh fears authorities could take new measures to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains, while Chile's peso slumped on falling copper prices.\par \par \uc2 As Brazil's local markets reopened after the Carnival holiday, the real <BRBY> bid at 1.655 per dollar, 0.73 percent weaker from its close last Friday at a 2-1/2-year high.\par \par \uc2 The real had then closed beyond what many see as the Finance Ministry's unofficial limit around 1.65 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 A ministry source told Reuters the government may announce a new round of measures this week aimed at curtailing the strong real.[ID:nN04241800]\par \par \uc2 Some analysts think Brazilian authorities could take more aggressive action than in the past. Flavia Cattan-Naslausky, an analyst at RBS Securities, said one option could be to raise a tax on foreign investments in equities.\par \par \uc2 "The risk is that they do something that is not very market-friendly," she said.\par \par \uc2 Last October the government tripled to 6 percent a tax on foreigners buying local bonds and trading in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives. The tax on equity investments held at 2 percent.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  has steadily escalated its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since 2009 as a tide of global investment was drawn to its double-digit interest rates. The flows pumped up the real by more than 40 percent since the beginning of 2009.\par \par \uc2 The stronger real is hurting local manufacturers who have to compete with cheapening imports. So far, Brazil's efforts to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  have slowed, but not deterred its advance.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <CLP=CL> lost 0.57 percent to 477.7 per dollar as copper prices fell. Higher crude oil prices worried investors that inflationary pressures could hit economic growth and demand for the industrial metal.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Michael O'Boyle; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110312e739000ks\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
