\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real hits 2-1/2 yr high, oil hits pesos\b0\par\par\uc2 601 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 19:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  breaks past key level, more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  eyed\par \par \uc2 * Oil price rise weighs on Mexican and Chilean pesos\par \par \uc2 * Brazil real gains 0.42 percent, Mexico peso flat\par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds comments)\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, March 4 (Reuters) - Brazil's real surged to its strongest in 2-1/2 years on Friday, pushing the government to contemplate new measures to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains next week.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's government may announce a new round of measures, possibly from the middle of next week, to tame the recent appreciation of the real, a finance ministry source told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The comments came after the real jumped during Friday's session despite a series of dollar auctions meant to slow its gains.\par \par \uc2 U.S. February jobs data improved on Friday, but not at a fast enough pace to disturb bets that the United States keep interest rates low, insuring cheap funding for market players who borrow dollars to invest in Brazilian assets. [ID:nN04228803]\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Brazil's annual inflation rate ticked up to upper limit of the government's target range, backing expectations that policy-makers will further tighten borrowing costs. [ID:nN04261260]\par \par \uc2 "We did not have particularly strong U.S. (job) numbers, even though the underlying picture is improving, you could continue to see flows attracted into markets such as Brazil," said David Mann, head of Americas research at Standard Chartered in New York.\par \par \uc2 Brazil raised its benchmark rate to 11.75 percent late Wednesday. With some of the highest yields in the world, a tide of yield-hungry global investors are pushing up the real, which notched a more than 1.1 percent gain this week and a 44 percent gain since 2009.\par \par \uc2 The real <BRBY> bid 0.42 percent stronger on Friday to 1.643 per dollar, its strongest since August 2008.\par \par \uc2 The strong real is hurting local manufacturers and authorities are using a tool box of dollar auctions and taxes to try and ward off the flows. On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deployed dollar auctions in both the forward and spot market.\par \par \uc2 When the real was trading around current levels last October, the finance ministry hiked taxes on foreign inflows.\par \par \uc2 "This is a key test right now and it remains to be seen if we will see more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  or if there is a retreat and a new line in the sand is yet to be drawn," Mann added.\par \par \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  told clients to bet of further gains in the real in the non-deliverable forwards market, where a position against the dollar could nab significant gains even if authorities manage to keep the real around current levels.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, renewed concerns about rising oil prices weighed on Mexico and Chile's pesos.\par \par \uc2 U.S. crude oil prices jumped amid clashes in Libya near a major oil terminal, reviving concerns that higher oil prices could weigh down global growth.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=> traded flat at 12.0050 per dollar, paring early gains that had taken it to a more than three week high.\par \par \uc2 While Mexico exports oil, it has been hurt by concerns that higher oil prices will weigh down consumer demand in the United States, which buys around 80 percent of local exports.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso <CLP=CL> lost 0.15 percent to 473.70 per dollar. Any slowdown in global growth will hurt demand for copper, the country's top export.\par \par \uc2 Chile also imports most of its oil, unlike exporter Mexico and self-sufficient Brazil.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110307e7340018f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
