\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED - EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil yields up, real firms as rate hike eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 600 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 18:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Corrects to remove reference in first paragraph to Chile's peso gaining)\par \par \uc2 * Brazil yields rise after surprise rise in IP data\par \par \uc2 * Market marginally raises bets on a 75 basis point hike\par \par \uc2 * Brazil real firms 0.18 pct, Mexico peso 0.26 pct\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, March 2 (Reuters) - Brazilian yields rose on Wednesday and the real firmed as surprisingly strong industrial data marginally backed bets for an aggressive interest rate hike, while Mexico's peso gained.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to raise its benchmark interest rate by at least 50 basis point later on Wednesday to 11.75 percent. Higher rates should bolster the real, but \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is containing gains. [ID:nN01145534]\par \par \uc2 Data showed \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's industrial production rose 0.2 percent in January, pushing up yields in the interest rate futures market <0#DIJ:> as investors bet policymakers could deliver a three-quarter-percentage point hike. [ID:nN02140898]\par \par \uc2 "The bets are a bit higher, but in absolute terms the probability of a 75 basis point hike is very small," said Diego Donadio, an analyst at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Inflation expectations have worsened since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's last 50-basis-point hike in January. But most economists think spending cuts by the new government and higher bank reserve requirements have eased pressure for a bigger hike.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> firmed 0.18 percent to 1.659 per dollar even after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held a dollar forward auction.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to firm despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and global jitters about higher oil prices as investors pile into the country's debt, which is offering among the highest interest rates in the world.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=> firmed 0.26 percent to 12.0890 per dollar as the greenback was pressured by expectations that interest rates in the euro zone will rise earlier than those in the United States.\par \par \uc2 "There is a general sentiment of dollar weakness since the U.S. seems more worried about the recovery than inflation, and other central banks could raise interest rates first," said Alejandro Martinez, a debt and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso gained about 5 percent from November to January on the back of an improving outlook for the U.S. economy, but concerns about the economic impact of higher oil prices have stalled the peso's rally.\par \par \uc2 "It will be difficult to see stronger gains, because risk appetite is really weak due to the situation in the Middle East. If oil prices remain high for a prolonged period, the United States economy could slow down, and that would hurt the peso," Martinez added.\par \par \uc2 Martinez said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely trade between 12.08 per dollar and 12.15 per dollar in the coming sessions.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso <CLP=CL> bid nearly flat at 476.30 per dollar, recovering from early losses as oil prices pulled back from session highs.\par \par \uc2 Worries that rising oil prices could weigh down global growth have hurt prices for copper, Chile's main export.\par \par \uc2 Chile also imports most of its oil, making it susceptible to a sustained spike in oil prices.\par \par \uc2 "If this happens, we could see the exchange rate around 480 per dollar. The market is focused on what happens with oil prices, which affects copper," said Sergio Tricio, head of research at \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chile.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Moises Avila in Santiago; Editing by Andrew Hay)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (CORRECTED)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110305e732000c5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
