\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  mixed; Chile peso hits 6-week high\b0\par\par\uc2 727 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Februar 2011\par 15:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Chile peso hits 6-week high after rate hike\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real contained by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Bets on Mexican peso hit highest since April 2010 (Rewrites throughout)\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Feb 18 (Reuters) - Chile's peso jumped to a six-week high on Friday as the market bet on more interest rate hikes and doubted authorities would step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts, while Mexico and \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost steam.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=CL> bid 0.26 percent stronger to 468.50 per dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates by 25 basis points to 3.5 percent, adding to the appeal of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . For details, see [ID:nN17302923]\par \par \uc2 A string of comments from Chilean officials also eased concerns that authorities will expand their efforts to contain the peso's gains after introducing a $50-million-a-day dollar purchase program at the beginning of January.\par \par \uc2 "There is a clear commitment to continue to fight inflation and we have heard from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board members that they will pay more attention to the inflation target than the exchange rate," said Bertrand Delgado, an economist at Roubini Global Economics in New York.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso racked up a 0.79 percent gain for the week, despite a sharp drop in the price of copper -- the country's main export -- which hurt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in the week.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely firm toward a nearly three-year high around 450 per dollar, "as long as nothing happens to the price of copper," Delgado said.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real <BRBY>, slipped 0.06 percent to 1.662 per dollar as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a narrow range.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held a forward auction and a reverse swap auction, both of which can weigh on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Policymakers were apparently reacting to a jump in the previous session, when the real posted sharp gains.\par \par \uc2 The lower house of Brazil's Congress shook off pressure from labor unions and approved the new administration's proposal for a small increase in the minimum wage late Wednesday, boosting confidence in the new government's clout.\par \par \uc2 The real has been trading in increasingly narrow ranges in recent weeks, slowed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but still steadily firming as investors are drawn to \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interest rates, among the highest in the world.\par \par \uc2 The real gained 0.18 percent in the last week.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=> slipped 0.12 percent on Friday to close at 12.023 per dollar, notching 0.08 percent gain for the week.\par \par \uc2 The peso ran into a brick wall at the psychologically key 12-per dollar after sharp gains on Thursday. Local companies have been heavy buyers of dollars around the 12 level.\par \par \uc2 Many local companies fixed their budgets for the year with expectations of a peso at 12.50 per dollar during 2011, making the 12-per-dollar level hard to resist.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso has been a favorite bet since last November, gaining more than 4 percent on an improving outlook for the United States, Mexico's main trading partner.\par \par \uc2 Delgado said the peso would need surprisingly strong data in the United States to break below 12 per dollar in the short term, but he said the peso would eventually firm toward 11.50.\par \par \uc2 Data from the Commodity Futures Trading Commission in Chicago showed on Friday that the net amount of bets in favor of the Mexican peso rose to their highest level since April 2010, according to Win Thin, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 "Everyone is really long and that makes me nervous," Thin said, noting the peso could be hit by any increase in global jitters related to political unrest in the Middle East or Europe's debt troubles. A spike in worries about Europe hammered the peso down from a high in May 2010.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso has the most bets in its favor of the eight major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracked by Reuters. [ID:nN18104672]\par \par \uc2 While that backs up the fundamental backdrop boding for futher gains, it also makes it vulnerable to any global shocks that could send speculators running for the door.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110221e72i000wf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
