\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's real firms, Chile peso trades flat\b0\par\par\uc2 392 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2011\par 15:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real rises after dropping three straight days\par \par \uc2 * Chilean peso trades flat ahead of cen bank's decision\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso nearly unchanged\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Feb 17 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed slightly in early trading on Thursday while Chile's peso traded nearly flat ahead of a possible rise in the country's interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> rose 0.12 percent to bid at 1.668 per dollar, after three consecutive declines but still within the narrow range of between 1.65 and 1.70 per dollar seen since the start of the year.\par \par \uc2 "The real continues in an environment of zero volatility. It has been totally hemmed in by governmental \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a treasurer at a foreign bank based in Sao Paulo.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stepped up its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  while investors have tried to push the real higher based on positive economic fundamentals and high interest rates that encourage the so-called carry trade.\par \par \uc2 The country has been a prime target for investors that borrow money cheaply in a country with lower interest rates to chase higher yields elsewhere. Brazil's interest rates are among the world's highest.\par \par \uc2 Congressional approval on Wednesday of a small increase in the minimum wage had a slight market impact as it came as expected, brokers said.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso <CLP=CL> was flat, bidding 473.80 against the U.S. dollar ahead of the country's decision on interest rates. In early trading it fell slightly, following a decline in prices of the country's top export, copper.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected to raise its benchmark rate <CLINTR=ECI> by 25 basis points to 3.5 percent on Thursday, thereby giving priority to inflation worries over its concerns about a strong peso hammering exporters. [nN17302923]\par \par \uc2 "All eyes on February's monetary policy decision today... Market pricing, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surveys and our forecast all agree that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will resume tightening this month following a pause in January," said \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in a report.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=> also traded flat, at 12.0645 per dollar. (Reporting by Silvio Cascione, Writing by Inae Riveras; Editing by Theodore d'Afflisio)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110220e72h000is\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
