\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Weaker Early Following Tepid Euro Data\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2011\par 13:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real weakened early in the session Monday as dissappointing data from the Euro-zone and a consequent weakening of the Euro set the tone for local trading.\par \par \uc2 The real opened at BRL1.6695 to the dollar after ending at BRL1.6660 to the dollar Friday according to \uc2 Telekurs\uc2  via Factset.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted the real slipped against the dollar as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracked the path of the euro following the release of discouraging December European industrial production data. European industrial production declined 0.1% from November, despite forecasts for a stable result. The industrial output data brought renewed focus on the region's recent debt woes and economic difficulties.\par \par \uc2 Adding to those concerns were disappointing data from Portugal, which posted a 0.3% contraction in the 4th quarter.\par \par \uc2 Locally, meanwhile, the market continues to monitor investment inflows to the Brazilian economy, which topped $15 billion in January.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect continued strong foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows, though much could depend on whether the government opts to use more mechanisms to restrict flows of dollars.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped up market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with forward dollar purchases and auctions of "reverse swaps," that allow investors to exchange dollar-indexed bonds for paper linked to domestic interest rates. The auctions are aimed at helping remove an excess of dollar-linked paper from the futures market.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, the bank is seen maintaining its weight in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Monday with customary daily dollar purchase auctions to build foreign reserves.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's reserves last week surpassed the $300 billion mark for the first time on record with a continued acquisition of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . .\par \par \uc2 -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; (5561) 3335-0832; gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 14-02-11 1223GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1836 5053 5076   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110214e72e0012t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
