\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Currency \highlight\uc2  Market Wilts Under Weight Of Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jeff Fick   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 570 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2011\par 19:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexed its muscles Monday in a series of moves that weighed heavily on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, taking a more aggressive tack in an effort to contain the real's appreciation against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 During Monday's session, the bank held two auctions to buy dollars on the spot market as well as the sale of forward dollar purchase contracts. The moves appeared to build on heavy dollar purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, traders said.\par \par \uc2 "The bank is certainly showing greater aggressiveness," said Alberto Orsovay, a dealer at Sao Paulo-based brokerage Hencorp Commcor.\par \par \uc2 Brazil has started 2011 with a concerted effort to contain the real's strength against the U.S. dollar, implementing heavy dollar purchases and other measures designed to stifle the wave of foreign investment flooding into Latin America's largest economy.\par \par \uc2 Investors seeking high rates of return have flocked to Brazil, lured by the country's towering interest rates and solid economic fundamentals. That has sent the real to gains of more than 30% against the greenback since the start of 2009.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  undercut the real Monday, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakening to BRL1.6755 to the dollar as of 1857 GMT, according to \uc2 Telekurs\uc2  via Factset. The real closed Friday at BRL1.6725 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Despite the real's weakness in the wake of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest moves, the broader trend remained tilted toward further appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to traders.\par \par \uc2 "It's complicated," Orsovay said. "Foreigners want to put money into Brazil, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to hold the line on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate to facilitate exports."\par \par \uc2 The primary culprit is Brazil's benchmark Selic base interest rate, which currently stands at 11.25%. Alexandre Tombini, the new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president, faces a tough task balancing new President Dilma Rousseff's pledge to lower interest rates with the bank's promise to fight inflation.\par \par \uc2 For now, inflation is dictating the fight. Inflation ended 2010 at 5.91%--the highest since 2004--and is expected to continue climbing in January. The Brazilian Census Bureau, or IBGE, will release January's IPCA consumer price index Tuesday, with economists polled by Dow Jones Newswires expecting a climb of 0.79%.\par \par \uc2 Many economists believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is already behind the curve in its fight against inflation and will need to raise interest rates further. That will attract even more attention from foreign investors and place additional pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, economists said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, is likely betting that aggressive action will bear fruit similar to what happened in January. Brazil registered dollar inflows of more than $12 billion in the first month of 2011, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sopped up more than $7 billion worth of greenbacks that helped stop the real from posting any appreciable gains for the month.\par \par \uc2 January's relative success means that Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will likely see a steady dose of the same measures--spot-market auctions, reverse swaps and forward-dollar contract sales--to keep the real stable in the face of steady inflows, Hencorp Commcor's Orsovay said.\par \par \uc2 -By Jeff Fick, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-21-2586-6085; Jeff.Fick@dowjones.com [ 07-02-11 1858GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110207e727001br\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
