\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Weakens Early Under Influence Of  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Presence\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2011\par 13:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real weakened at the outset of trading Monday as the threat of a continued heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  presence held sway over the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The real opened at BRL1.6760 to the dollar after ending at BRL1.6720 to the dollar Friday according to \uc2 Telekurs\uc2  via Factset.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared at least temporarily to be making some headway in influencing the direction of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after taking a forceful stand in the market in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 Alongside the effects of a wilting local equities market, the bank on Friday opted two spot market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchase auctions and also called a surprise auction of reverse swap auction at which it sold 71% of the 20,000 contracts on offer for around $707 million.\par \par \uc2 For Monday's session, meanwhile, the bank announced it would hold three forward dollar auctions to offer contracts with maturities of Feb. 16, Feb. 23 and March 9.\par \par \uc2 The latest \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been part of a tireless campaign by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and government to offset the impact of widely available global liquidity and heavy incoming foreign investment in Brazil, which has helped strengthen the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by more than 30% against the dollar over the past 24 months.\par \par \uc2 The strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has hurt exports and encouraged more imports from abroad, thus slimming the country's foreign trade surplus.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen maintaining weight in the spot market Monday with more daily dollar purchase auctions to build foreign reserves.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's reserves as of Friday stood at $299.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; (5561) 3335-0832, gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 07-02-11 1231GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1836 5053 5076   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110207e7270011i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
