\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Mkts Spend Big On  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  Amid Dubious Success\b0\par\par\uc2 853 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2011\par 17:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 -Emerging-Market \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Rising Despite \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 -Effectiveness of \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  Seen As Mixed\par \par \uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  Bring Costs Of Soaking Up Excess Liquidity\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Erin McCarthy and Anjali Cordeiro \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging-market countries have been undertaking costly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to hold down the value of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but how effective these efforts have been in containing investment inflows is debatable.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Countries from Brazil to South Korea have raised their reserves, taxed outside investments or instituted other types of capital controls to prevent foreign inflows from driving up their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Yet the success in halting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation remains hard to gauge, with the focus more on slowing the rate of increase rather than on reversing it. At the same time, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have imposed a battery of hidden costs on these countries' central banks and capital markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In Brazil, where taxes have been placed on various types of foreign flows and where the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been buying up U.S. dollars on a nearly daily basis, the real has generally stayed on an upward path. It was at BRL1.6722 recently, according to CQG, putting it up roughly 1.7% since increased taxes were announced on outside investments in October.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  strategist Maya Hernandez estimated that the real might have strengthened to as much as BRL1.50 to the dollar, without the policy moves.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There is a limit to how much [countries] can \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," she said. "So, going forward, the best \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can hope for is stability [in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ] or a slowdown in the pace of appreciation," she said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In South Korea, policymakers have implemented a cap on banks' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  forward positions and imposed a levy against banks' balance of nondeposit foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  debt. Still, the won has been strengthening lately, recently reaching about KRW1115 to the dollar, compared with KRW1165 in mid-December.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Korea has tried it and it's [apparently] not working but who knows where we'd be without [the policy moves]," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brown Brothers Harriman\f28 \uc2 \f2  strategist Win Thin.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some argue that these policies can backfire even with regards to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's valuation. For instance, Nomura Securities strategist Tony Volpon argued that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have reduced volatility in its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market and so have made its super high-yielding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the real, even more attractive to outside investors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "This is actually making the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  a better bet and is generating inflows that I don't think would have been there if there had been more actual volatility," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What is more, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets can be expensive for central banks, which must issue interest-bearing bonds to soak up the excess local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  liquidity that is created in the process.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continues to purchase a mix of euros and dollars, which pay rates of around 1.5% to 2%, it has to offset the added market liquidity by issuing debt at an average local cost of 11%. That 9% shortfall on its reserves amounts to "a very big negative carry," said Nomura's Volpon. "They're really stretching the edge of the envelope by this kind of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ." He estimated that the costs of sterilization for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may have reached up to 40 billion Brazilian reais in 2010.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chile in January launched a $12 billion \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program. That \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been more successful because it had a "combined coordinated policy response," Volpon said. Chile initiated a large dollar-purchasing program and at the same time held interest rates steady in January. According to CQG, the Chilean peso has weakened to CLP479.05 to the dollar, compared to a close of CLP466.65 on Jan. 3.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As with Chile, Colombia has also made several moves to weaken its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , including making daily dollar purchases of at least $20 million and placing restrictions on public-sector flows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Beyond building their reserves, emerging markets in Asia and Latin America have taken other steps. Taiwan last year tightened restrictions on foreign investments in certain short-term local-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  products. In October, Thailand imposed a tax on income that foreign investors could earn on Thai bonds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While capital controls can be cheaper to implement, they can also have far-reaching effects on investor sentiment. While the jitters that they create among investors might help in keeping speculators away in the short term, the longer-term impact on sentiment is hard to gauge.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Investors are getting spooked," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brown Brothers Harriman\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Thin. "What if [the restrictions] get out of control? If you prick investor confidence, it's hard to get it back."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, inflation pressure is becoming more of a headache for emerging markets everywhere, a development that will make it even more complicated for policymakers looking to fight price pressures and keep their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from rising too much. By raising rates to battle inflation, policymakers risk pushing up their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  even more.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Erin McCarthy and Anjali Cordeiro; Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2200; anjali.cordeiro@dowjones.com [ 04-02-11 1625GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020110204e72400014\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
