\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Brazil industry shrinks in Dec as  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  weighs\b0\par\par\uc2 688 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2011\par 12:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Industrial output contracts 0.7 pct in December from Nov\par \par \uc2 * Production up 10.5 pct in 2010, biggest gain since 1986\par \par \uc2 * Yields on interest rate futures fall on industry data (Recasts, adds analyst comments, interest rate futures)\par \par \uc2 By Elzio Barreto\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Feb 2 (Reuters) - Industrial production in Brazil unexpectedly fell in December from the previous month, ending the year on a sour note as manufacturers struggle with a strong real and a flood of cheap imports.\par \par \uc2 The surprise contraction could signal a slowdown in Latin America's largest economy and help ease pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to increase interest rates to cool growth and inflation. Yields on interest rate futures <0#DIJ:> fell after the data were released.\par \par \uc2 Industrial output fell 0.7 percent in December from November <BRIO=ECI>, while November figures were revised lower to a 0.2 percent decline from a drop of 0.1 percent, statistics agency IBGE said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The weak figures could spark calls for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more aggressively in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real <BRBY> from gaining further. A strong real is making local products expensive compared to imports and making it harder for Brazilian exporters to sell goods abroad.\par \par \uc2 The real firmed 4.6 percent in 2010, on top of a 34 percent rally the previous year, spurring a jump in imports and prompting analysts at \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  to call it the world's most overvalued major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Despite an otherwise strong economy -- surging retail sales, record-low unemployment and rising wages -- the industry data suggest that foreign manufacturers are increasingly reaping the benefits of Brazil's consumption boom.\par \par \uc2 "The very weak performance at the end of the year justifies the concerns by the government and manufacturers about the very strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Luciano Rostagno, chief strategist at brokerage CM Capital Markets in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 "Amid strong consumption in the country, production is just not responding."\par \par \uc2 Despite the decline in December, industrial output climbed 10.5 percent for the whole of 2010, the biggest annual gain since 1986, the IBGE said. In 2009, when Brazil was recovering from a brief recession, production slumped 7.4 percent.\par \par \uc2 Yields on Brazilian interest rate futures fell across the board on Wednesday as investors reduced bets for an increase in borrowing costs in the months ahead. With Brazil's rates already among the world's highest, an increase in borrowing costs could lure more capital into the country and increase pressure on the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The yield on the contract due July 2011 <DIJN1>, one of the most heavily-traded contracts of the session, dipped to 11.90 percent from 11.91 percent late on Tuesday. The yield on the contract due January 2012 <DIJF2> fell to 12.34 percent from 12.38 percent.\par \par \uc2 INDUSTRIAL SECTORS\par \par \uc2 Production had been expected to rise 0.85 percent in December from November, according to the median estimate of 12 analysts in a Reuters survey. Forecasts for the increase ranged from of 0.4 percent to 1.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 Among industrial sectors surveyed, 11 posted a decline in production, led by a 13.3 percent slump in electronic materials and communications equipment. Fifteen sectors increased output, including office material and computers and chemical products.\par \par \uc2 In broader industrial categories, output of capital goods fell 0.5 percent in December from November. Production of consumer goods dropped 0.9 percent month on month, while durable consumer goods output slipped 0.6 percent.\par \par \uc2 Industrial production climbed 2.7 percent in December compared with the same month in 2009 <BRIOY=ECI>, far less than the 5.3 percent median forecast in the Reuters survey. Estimates ranged from 4.5 percent to 6.9 percent.\par \par \uc2 For details on the IBGE industrial output figures see: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.ibge.gov.br/home/presidencia/noticias/noticia_visualiza.php?id_noticia=1811&id_pagina=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.ibge.gov.br/home/presidencia/noticias/noticia_visualiza.php?id_noticia=1811&id_pagina=1}}}\uc2  (Additional reporting by Denise Luna and Rodrigo Viga Gaier, Editing by Todd Benson and W Simon)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-ECONOMY/INDUSTRY (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110202e722000rp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
