\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Slightly Weaker On Egypt, Euro Zone Inflation\b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2011\par 13:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real was trading slightly weaker against the U.S. dollar early Wednesday on Euro Zone inflation worries and continued uncertainties surrounding the Egyptian political crisis.\par \par \uc2 Early in the session, the real was trading at BRL1.6648 to the dollar, according to \uc2 Telekurs\uc2  via Factset. The real ended Tuesday's session at BRL1.6625.\par \par \uc2 The Egyptian political crisis has led to wobbly \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and commodities markets worldwide. For Brazil, the crisis has meant an increase in risk aversion by global investors.\par \par \uc2 "The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is basically in wait-and-see mode," said a Sao Paulo trader who wished not to be named. "We're waiting to see how the Egyptian crisis plays out."\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Euro Zone's producer price index, released earlier Wednesday, showed a 0.8% rise in December over November, the biggest jump in two years. The 12-month figure was 5.3%, fueling ideas that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to hike interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Higher European interest rates would tend to divert global investors from emerging markets like Brazil toward Europe.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian market is also overshadowed by the possibility of fresh government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently in the market in recent months in a frank attempt to stem the appreciation of the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The strong real hurts Brazilian exports.\par \par \uc2 "At any moment, the government can call an auction to soak up dollar liquidity," said the Sao Paulo trader.\par \par \uc2 -By Tom Murphy, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3544-7090;\par \par \uc2 brazil@dowjones.com [ 02-02-11 1226GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110202e722000yl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
