\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil, Chile  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  hit 1-mo highs\b0\par\par\uc2 608 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2011\par 15:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil real, Chilean pesos hit nearly 1-month highs\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso firms 1 pct, below 12/dlr level\par \par \uc2 * Strong U.S. manufacturing data boosts growth hopes\par \par \uc2 * Brazil real firms 0.6 pct (Recasts; adds comment, updates closing prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jean Luis Arce and Elzio Barreto\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY/SAO PAULO(Reuters) - Brazil's and Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit nearly one-month highs Tuesday and Mexico's peso broke the 12 per dollar level after surveys showed global factories were gaining steam in January.\par \par \uc2 Bets that Brazil and Chile will raise interest rates to cool strong growth and rising inflation have boosted the allure of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite major \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  programs.\par \par \uc2 A survey released Tuesday showed the U.S. manufacturing sector expanded at its fastest pace in almost seven years in January, following similar surveys showing growth in Europe's and China's factories.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso, which closely tracks the outlook for the U.S. economy, led gains with a more than 1 percent surge to strengthen past the psychological 12-per-dollar level.\par \par \uc2 "There was good data in Europe and good data in the United States that are helping the whole risk trade," said Ramses Villela, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Bulltick Capital Markets in Mexico City, referring to bets on assets like stocks, emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and commodities.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso bid 0.69 percent firmer at 479.70 per U.S. dollar, driven by a record price for copper, the country's main export.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso has gained around 4 percent against the dollar in since mid-January, cutting back into the 7 percent loss it suffered after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  early last month.\par \par \uc2 BACK BELOW 12\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso firmed 1.04 percent to 11.99 per dollar, nearing an almost 2-1/2-year high hit last month.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso has gained more than 4 percent from a November intraday low as improving U.S. economic data promises to support solid demand for Mexico's exports.\par \par \uc2 A monthly poll showed that analysts following Mexico's economy raised their expectations for both growth and inflation this year. But some analysts said the stronger peso will curb the need for an interest rate hike in Mexico.\par \par \uc2 "We believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation will absorb the inflation pressures from higher food prices and therefore allow (Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to leave the policy rate unchanged throughout the year," wrote Benito Berber, an analyst at Nomura in New York, in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 Mexico placed 25 billion pesos ($2.08 billion) of a new 10-year bond Tuesday with a yield of 7.44 percent.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real gained in spite of heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the previous session by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which held three dollar-forward auctions and two spot-dollar auctions in a bid to undermine the real's strength.\par \par \uc2 "The combination of lower risk aversion and expectations of higher rates in Brazil beats anything they put there," said Pedro Tuesta, senior Latin America economist at research firm 4Cast Inc in Washington. "Money is still pouring in."\par \par \uc2 Brazil's economy is posting solid growth and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen raising its benchmark interest rates from 11.25 percent to 12.50 percent by year-end, boosting the appeal of local assets to yield-hungry investors.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real was bid 0.6 percent stronger at 1.662 per U.S. dollar on the local spot market. (Additional reporting and writing by Michael O'Boyle; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110204e721001h9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
