\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil, Mexico  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  hit 2-wk low on Egypt\b0\par\par\uc2 699 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2011\par 15:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil calls first-ever \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards auction\par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso, Brazil real hit around 2-week lows\par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso loses 1.3 pct, Brazil's real 0.36 pct\par \par \uc2 * Chile's peso up 1.8 pct in week on rate hike bets (Recasts to reflect reversal in region's markets)\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle and Samantha Pearson\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY/SAO PAULO, Jan 28 (Reuters) - Global jitters over political unrest in Egypt drove Mexico's peso and Brazil's real on Friday to their weakest levels in about two weeks as investors dumped riskier assets across the board.\par \par \uc2 Egypt's president imposed curfews in the country as anti-government protests turned violent, sparking fears about similar unrest across the Middle East, which could lead to higher oil prices that could hurt global growth. For details, see [ID:nLDE70Q2OZ]\par \par \uc2 "Above all there were rumors that they could close the Suez Canal, that would hit trade and the region and get passed on around the world," said Mario Copca, an analyst at brokerage Vanguardia in Mexico City. "If they manage to calm down the social unrest over the weekend, we will surely see a big bounce back in markets," he added.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said months of solid gains in riskier assets like emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks had set markets up to be quick to take profits on any surprisingly negative news. Before Friday's losses, the Mexican peso was up about 4 percent against the dollar from an intraday low in November.\par \par \uc2 "The market was ripe for a correction," said Jorge Perez-Duarte, a managing director for emerging markets at \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  in Toronto. "Hopefully this will not turn out to be anything bigger than a healthy correction."\par \par \uc2 The real <BRBY> gave up early gains to trade 0.36 percent weaker at 1.683 reais per U.S. dollar on the local spot market, its weakest level since Jan. 14.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> fell 1.31 percent to 12.1950 per dollar to trade at its weakest since January 11. It was the worst one-day loss for the peso since late November, when it began to rally on an improving outlook for the economy in the United States, its top trading partner.\par \par \uc2 However, the Chilean peso <CLP=>, which closed trading before the worst of Friday's global losses, gained 0.17 pct to 484.20. The peso gained 1.8 percent during the week to trade at its strongest since a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program at the beginning of January.\par \par \uc2 The peso has been backed by bets that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will resume hiking interest rates next month after pausing in January to complement the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program. [ID:nN13283103]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 BRAZIL\b0 \highlight\uc2 'S REAL PROBLEMS\par \par \uc2 The events in Egypt had a more significant impact on Brazil's real than earlier attempts by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday said it will buy dollar forwards via three separate auctions on Monday, the latest in a series of technical measures to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent rise. [ID:nN28245256]\par \par \uc2 The real barely budged after the announcement.\par \par \uc2 "If you just think about the number of IPOs (initial public offerings) in the works, the amount of cash which came into Brazil during the last few days, the last month ... there is not much you can do," said Joao Medeiros, a partner at Pioneer Corretora, one of Brazil's biggest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  brokerages.\par \par \uc2 Other analysts were skeptical about the nature of the auctions. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would auction contracts for the following settlement dates: Feb. 9, 16 and 23.\par \par \uc2 "I have strong doubts about the forward auctions because they are all being called on Wednesdays and the inflows won't necessarily happen on those days," said Alfredo Barbutti, an economist at the BGC Liquidez brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 If the market gets used to them every Wednesday, investors will also find a way around them, he said. (Additional reporting by Noe Torres in Mexico City; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110131e71s001j9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
