\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's real up despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  move\b0\par\par\uc2 713 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2011\par 14:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says could buy dollar forwards\par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real adds 0.1 pct, Mexican peso up 0.4 pct\par \par \uc2 * Chile's peso gains 0.6 pct as copper price surges (Adds comments from Chile, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Nathalia Ferreira\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Jan 26 (Reuters) - Brazil's real firmed on Wednesday despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest effort to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation and protect local manufacturers.\par \par \uc2 The bank said late on Tuesday that for the first time ever it could offer \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards at auction. The auctions would be similar to those currently conducted in the spot market but the contracts would be settled at a date in the future. [ID:nN25294325]\par \par \uc2 But the Brazilian real <BRBY> barely reacted, bidding 0.12 percent stronger at 1.667 reais per U.S. dollar on the local spot market.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican and Chilean pesos were also firmer on Wednesday as the dollar weakened broadly following U.S. President Barack Obama's promise of spending cuts. [ID:nLDE70P0HM]\par \par \uc2 Data showing U.S. single-family home sales in December rose to their highest in eight months also helped to boost the peso.\par \par \uc2 Economists and traders said one reason for the real's muted reaction to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's assault was that it was not clear exactly how often these auctions would be called and the reason behind them.\par \par \uc2 "If there is some specific deal, if there is going to be an inflow from 'company X' on Wednesday next week for example, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  already knows about it and it could use this measure," said Alfredo Barbutti, an economist at the BGC Liquidez brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 "But the intention behind this measure is still not clear...if the point is to control the exchange rate then it would be better to just use reverse swaps as they have a more direct effect."\par \par \uc2 Also, the forwards market is tiny compared to Brazil's spot and futures market. As such, they said, this latest measure is more likely to be an attempt to close off a loophole and make the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy more efficient.\par \par \uc2 "Judging how the liquidity is concentrated between the spot market (average US$2bln daily) and the futures market (as much as 7 times that) with the forward market much smaller...the measure should not have much of an impact," said Flavia Cattan-Naslausky, a strategist at RBS Securities in New York, in a research note.\par \par \uc2 "The decision looks like an effort to close a loophole to capture all sides of the market," she added.\par \par \uc2 Thirdly, Brazil still remains an attractive place to invest and the real will continue to appreciate until the authorities introduce drastic measures such as widespread quarantines or capital controls, they said.\par \par \uc2 "The next instrument (to be announced) could be some type of restriction on a specific inflow, something like the quarantine," said Jorge Lima, a consultant at Previbank DTVM in Sao Paulo. "But Brazil can't shut itself off from long-term investment, so it would have to be a very specific restriction on speculative transactions."\par \par \uc2 WEAK DOLLAR BOOSTS REGION\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> strengthened 0.43 percent to 12.045 per dollar in early trading, as the greenback weakened broadly.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> firmed 0.57 percent to 489.90 per dollar as the price of copper, the country's main export, surged due to the weaker dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The peso is strengthening because of a better performance by European stocks, copper has also recovered and the euro is maintaining an upward tendency," said Rodrigo Sarria, a trader at Celfin Capital in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 " With the markets so positive, the tendency is for the peso to keep firming" he added.\par \par \uc2 The greenback was suffering after a promise of spending cuts from U.S. President Barack Obama late on Tuesday cemented expectations the Fed will retain faith in its ultra-loose policy.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Moises Avila in Santiago) (Editing by Theodore d'Afflisio) (samantha.pearson@thomsonreuters.com; Reuters Messaging: samantha.pearson.thomsonreuters.com@reuters.net; +5511-5644-7736)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110129e71q0008j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
