\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  steps up  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  with forwards\b0\par\par\uc2 447 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2011\par 01:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  cenbank to offer \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards for first time\par \par \uc2 * Forward auctions add to moves to curb real's rally (Adds analyst comments, more details on cenbank measure)\par \par \uc2 By Elzio Barreto\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Tuesday it could offer \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards in market auctions for the first time ever, adding to several moves in recent weeks to help curb a rally in the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bank said only financial firms already registered as dealers in its electronic system may participate in the auctions.\par \par \uc2 Just like its regular \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the bank will call the forward auctions and will unveil terms of the transactions, with the key difference that contracts are settled at a future date.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, firmed 4.6 percent last year against the dollar, following gains of 34 percent in 2009, raising concerns among executives and government officials about the effects on local exporters and a flood of cheap imports into the country. The surge has prompted \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  recently to dub the real the world's most overvalued major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began selling reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps on Jan. 14 for the first time since May 2009. The swaps, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivative that effectively allows the bank to buy U.S. dollars on the futures market, came on top of an increase in reserve requirements on banks' short U.S. dollar positions and its daily spot market auctions.\par \par \uc2 "They've announce so many tools, it's looking like a patchwork of measures," said Pedro Tuesta, senior Latin America economist at research firm 4Cast Inc in Washington. "It seems they feel they are losing the battle, that's why they keep adding more tools."\par \par \uc2 "It looks like they are finding holes and putting their fingers in the dam, but then another hole comes up and they have to put another finger," he added.\par \par \uc2 Like several emerging economies, Brazil has had to tackle a flood of cheap capital from abroad as rates in the United States, Japan and other developed nations hover close to zero. Countries including South Korea, Taiwan, Peru and Turkey have taken several measures to stop speculative capital inflows that are aiming for higher yields in emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  headache will likely last for a while, with private money flowing into emerging markets seen reaching more than $1 trillion by 2012, the Institute of International Finance global bank group said on Monday. The IIF warned it may become harder for countries to reduce the effects of the flood of capital.\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110129e71q0000n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
