\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Latin America  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  may be here to stay\b0\par\par\uc2 766 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2011\par 20:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 * Commodity prices, Chinese demand to pressure \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real would be 10 pct firmer without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Measures more acceptable because of Chile, China\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Brad Haynes\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/SANTIAGO (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tame Latin America's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be here to stay as strong Chinese demand for commodities and rising inflation make governments reluctant to cede control over their markets.\par \par \uc2 Brazil, Peru, Colombia and even Chile's conservative authorities have aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  over recent months, surprising nerve-racked investors with an arsenal of measures.\par \par \uc2 Politicians such as Brazil's finance minister have blamed the rallies on the developed world, slamming the United States for keeping interest rates low and the dollar weak through its quantitative easing policy.\par \par \uc2 But rising Chinese demand for many of Latin America's key exports is likely to support commodity prices even as the dollar recovers, pushing the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to new highs and maintaining the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "There's a long-term case for Chinese demand as a fundamental element underpinning Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," says Enrique Alvarez, head of Latin American research at IDEAglobal in New York.\par \par \uc2 "This has become one of the major driving forces for Latin American economies, especially those that export traditional commodity-based materials such as Brazil, Argentina, Chile, Peru, Colombia -- just about the entire gamut of Latin American countries."\par \par \uc2 China's trade with Latin America grew ten-fold between 2000 and 2007, according to the U.S. Congressional Research Service, and in 2009 the Asian giant overtook the United States to become Brazil's top trading partner.\par \par \uc2 Higher inflation, partly as a result of a global surge in commodity prices and food costs, is also likely to force policymakers to raise interest rates across the region, boosting \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  further.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to hike its benchmark interest rate by 50 basis points to 11.25 percent later Wednesday to curb inflation, currently at a six-year high.\par \par \uc2 Chile is also set to raise lending costs in coming months.\par \par \uc2 "As the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps raising its benchmark rate and attracting foreign investment, it's likely that we'll see additional (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) measures," said Alejandro Puente, an economist with BBVA Chile in Santiago.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 : THE NEW NORM?\par \par \uc2 Although countries such as \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  are working on long-term solutions to bring down interest rates and relieve pressure on their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to remain a popular and necessary option in the meantime.\par \par \uc2 Without such measures, the Brazilian real and the Chilean peso would now be trading around 10 percent stronger at 1.50 and 450 per dollar respectively, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 "Lock-up" periods on foreign capital could be imposed in Brazil while countries such as Colombia may choose to extend dollar purchases.\par \par \uc2 "Oh \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  does work! It may not change the theoretical value of where the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be but in the short-term it absolutely does have an impact on markets," says Michael Woolfolk, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNY Mellon in New York.\par \par \uc2 The difficulty of exiting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies is amplified by their beggar-thy-neighbor nature.\par \par \uc2 Many \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators make money via regional cross trades (buying one Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against another), which means whichever country ditches \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  first risks luring the wave of cash washing around the continent.\par \par \uc2 Before Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shocked investors earlier this month with a $12 billion dollar-buying plan, many banks were advising buying the peso against the Brazilian real. Those same banks then advised clients to buy the Mexican peso against Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , driving Mexico's peso to a two-year high this week. Now speculation is rising Mexico may also have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to match its neighbors' aggressive efforts.\par \par \uc2 The proliferation of such policies has also made them more acceptable among investors, giving countries little incentive to ditch them prematurely.\par \par \uc2 "Chile gave \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  more respectability because its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has long held the view that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not successful in the medium term and that the (19)90s capital controls had limited impact at best," says Pedro Tuesta, senior Latin America economist at 4Cast Inc in Washington.\par \par \uc2 China's growing economic clout, achieved despite its fixed-rate \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, could also be changing the rules of the game globally, says Paul Biszko, senior strategist at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  in Toronto.\par \par \uc2 "There is the view that: China is doing it, the United States is doing it indirectly, why can't we do it?!" (Editing by Stuart Grudgings and Andrew Hay)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 BRAZIL\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|FUN  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110119e71j001q1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
