\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Currency \highlight\uc2  Market Eyes  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ,  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Move\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jeff Fick   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 528 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Januar 2011\par 20:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market joined in the ebullient mood coming out of Europe on Tuesday, but cast a wary eye at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's heavy hand ahead of \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first meeting of 2011.\par \par \uc2 Global markets got a boost earlier in the session from a series of successful bond sales by European Union member countries, including Belgium, Greece, Hungary and Spain, traders said. Brazil's real joined the euro and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to post solid gains against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 Tensions surrounding the debt and fiscal crisis in Europe appear to be waning, placing investor focus back on fundamentals. Thanks to sky-high interest rates and a booming economy, Brazil has enjoyed a select position among investors seeking high returns.\par \par \uc2 The real has reflected the return to normal in recent sessions, continuing a relentless appreciation that has seen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthen more than 30% against the dollar since the start of 2009. As of 1850 GMT, the real traded at BRL1.6745, stronger from Monday's close at BRL1.6800, according to \uc2 Telekurs\uc2  via Factset.\par \par \uc2 The real's strength has drawn the attention from new President Dilma Rousseff's administration, including new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Alexandre Tombini. As the real approached the BRL1.67 to the dollar mark Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  quickly acted by holding two spot-market auctions to snap up dollars.\par \par \uc2 The bank purchased an undisclosed volume of dollars at BRL1.6727 and BRL1.6758 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The return of daily double dollar auctions followed last week's reverse-swap auction, the first held by the bank since May 2009. The reverse-swap auctions allow investors to swap \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions in futures markets for government paper linked to interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Quick action has so far been the calling card of Brazil's government under Rousseff. In two swift moves under her leadership, Brazil has forced banks to make compulsory reserve deposits on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures contracts and allowed the country's Sovereign Wealth Fund to operate in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives market. The measures were designed to stem further appreciation of the real against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's booming economy, however, is undercutting the administration's ability to use capital measures to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely raise interest rates Wednesday because of increasing inflationary pressures.\par \par \uc2 The country ended 2010 with an inflation rate of 5.9%, well above the government's year-end target of 4.5%. The government maintained the 4.5% target for 2011, but analysts and economists expect prices to once again top that figure.\par \par \uc2 While a rate hike is seen as necessary to contain rising prices, it will also prove a powerful lure for foreign investors seeking higher rates of return. Economists polled by Dow Jones Newswires expect the bank's Copom rate-setting panel to raise the benchmark Selic base interest rate by a half-percentage point to 11.25%.\par \par \uc2 -By Jeff Fick, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-21-2586-6085, Jeff.Fick@dowjones.com [ 18-01-11 1904GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110118e71i001fa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
