\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Bank To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  In BRL\b0\par\par\uc2 1,325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2011\par 11:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1033 GMT [Dow Jones] The Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will step up its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets on Friday, moving into derivatives for the first time in more than 18 months with an auction to buy up to $1 billion in futures contracts. The BCB will be \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in BRL via the forward market. Its ability to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the spot has been dampened somewhat by recent regulations limiting banks' short USD spot positions, Banco Santander says in a research report. (rogerio.jelmayer@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 UBS\uc2  says it's bought USD/CHF at 0.9630 with a target of 1.02 and a protective stop at 0.9430. Why, because the bank thinks the U.S. economy is picking up speed, the market still seems to be long of the franc, the rate itself is not far from its all time lows and Switzerland is becoming more concerned about exchange rate strength. \uc2 UBS\uc2  says the risks to this trade are that U.S. data disappoints and German and Swiss data stays firm. USD/CHF now at 0.9641, the all-time low was 0.9301 seen on the last trading day of 2010. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1023 GMT [Dow Jones] India bonds fall on fears of imminent monetary tightening by the RBI after China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hikes banks' reserve requirement ratio by 50 bps, says a dealer with a state-run bank. The 8.08% 2022 bond is at 99.15 vs its day's high of 99.44 and compared with Thursday's close of 99.54. "The China decision on reserve requirement hike reinforces the fear of similar action by the RBI, going forward there could be further sell off," he says. Earlier in the session a INR110 billion auction of government bonds was fully subscribed as yields came in at expected levels. The dealer tips the 8.08% 2022 yield in a 8.16%-8.21% band.(sourav.mishra@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1022 GMT [Dow Jones] Poland's Monetary Policy Council, or MPC, will leave rates unchanged next week, despite hawkish statements of a number of the panel, including the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's head, BRE Bank's economist Marcin Mazurek says. He adds the purpose of the statements--to strengthen the zloty--has already been achieved. "The statements' impact was similar to 25 basis point to 50 basis point rate hike," Mazurek added. (malgorzata.halaba@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1020 GMT [Dow Jones] The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's full-year \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate-related losses could top CHF30 billion following further CHF gains versus the euro in the fourth quarter, says \uc2 Bank Sarasin\uc2 . "The \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses reached CHF21 billion in the first nine months, and an additional CHF10 billion loss in 4Q is feasible," says economist Ursina Kubli. The SNB is due to release its full-year earnings at 1630 GMT, and the net book loss, which also includes income from trading and higher gold reserve valuations could top CHF10 billion, from CHF8.5 billion in the first nine months, she points out. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1019 GMT [Dow Jones] In the wake of China's 50 basis point RRR hike the commodity trio of AUD, NZD and CAD have slipped to the day's lows vs the USD of 0.9880, 0.7637 and 0.9969 respectively. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1013 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/INR edges up after the PBOC hikes its reserve requirement by 50 bps, sparking fresh concern that global growth may be slowed by aggressive Chinese monetary policy moves, says a trader with a foreign bank. The pair is at 45.42 vs 45.38 before the announcement. "Local stock market sentiment has been weak over the last few weeks, and this will just add to the bearishness on the rupee," the trader says. He expects the pair to remain below 45.50 in the session, but continue to rally next week. (bijou.george@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1011 GMT [Dow Jones] China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday says it will raise the reserve requirement ratio for banks by 50 basis points from Thursday, Jan. 20; this is its latest tightening move and its first RRR hike this year, after six RRR hikes and two interest rate hikes late last year. The move adds to government efforts to manage excessive liquidity and contain inflation, as officials warn factors including loose monetary policies in other countries and rising international resource prices are adding to price pressures in China. (owen.fletcher@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1008 GMT [Dow Jones] Treasurys fall in London, with bunds also paring gains as tightening peripheral yield spreads reduce the appeal of safe haven debt. Sentiment for the euro zone periphery is also being supported by ongoing chatter on changes to the size and the mandate of the EFSF. Reaction to a 50bps reserve requirement hike by the PBOC has been muted. Friday sees a string of data releases, with CPI and advance retail sales at 1330 GMT. Industrial production figures are out at 1415 GMT while the University of Michigan consumer survey is out at 1455 GMT. The 2-year note is down at 100-00+/32, yielding 0.615%, the 10-year note is down at 94-07+/32, yielding 3.316%, and the 30-year bond is lower at 95-22+/32, yielding 4.512%, according to Tradeweb. March bunds are up 0.06 at 124.70 and March gilts are down 0.10 at 117.55. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1007 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares snap a 2-day winning streak to end down 0.3% at 1032.26 on profit-taking in active trade. Weakness in most regional bourses also dampens market sentiment. Big cap energy, banking stocks fall after their recent gains. "Prospects over the (Thai) stock market improve after it successfully stays above the support level at 1027," says an analyst with Ayudhya Securities Adisak Phupiphathirungul; investors should keep their eyes on any developments in the euro-zone. He tips resistance at 1044. Among top actives, \uc2 Indorama Ventures\uc2  (IVL.TH) is off 1.1% at THB45.75, PTT Chemical (PTTCH.TH) is up 0.7% at THB150, Thai Oil (TOP.TH) falls 2.0% to THB74.75, \uc2 Siam Commercial Bank\uc2  (SCB.TH) is down 1.5% at THB99.50 and IRPC (IRPC.TH) slips 0.8% to THB5.95. (oranan.paweewun@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1007 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares snap a 2-day winning streak to end down 0.3% at 1032.26 on profit-taking in active trade. Weakness in most regional bourses also dampens market sentiment. Big cap energy, banking stocks fall after their recent gains. "Prospects over the (Thai) stock market improve after it successfully stays above the support level at 1027," says an analyst with Ayudhya Securities Adisak Phupiphathirungul; investors should keep their eyes on any developments in the euro-zone. He tips resistance at 1044. Among top actives, \uc2 Indorama Ventures\uc2  (IVL.TH) is off 1.1% at THB45.75, PTT Chemical (PTTCH.TH) is up 0.7% at THB150, Thai Oil (TOP.TH) falls 2.0% to THB74.75, \uc2 Siam Commercial Bank\uc2  (SCB.TH) is down 1.5% at THB99.50 and IRPC (IRPC.TH) slips 0.8% to THB5.95. (oranan.paweewun@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1005 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD is firmer pretty much across the board after China says it will hike its Bank Reserve Requirements rate by 50 basis points effective January 20th. AUD/USD falls to the day's low of 0.9903 from around 0.9930, EUR/USD falls by the same margin to 1.3355 while USD/JPY EUR climbs to the day's high of 82.93. (gary.stride@dowjones.com) [ 01-14-11 0533ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110114e71e0007e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
