\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-EMERGING MARKETS-Mexican peso hits 8-month high, Brazil lags\b0\par\par\uc2 641 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2011\par 22:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 (Repeats to additional subscribers)\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso gains 0.6 pct, Chilean peso up 0.6 pct\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real dips 0.06 pct as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears weigh (Adds comments, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, Jan 11 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso jumped to an 8-month high on Tuesday, helped by surprisingly strong local industrial output data.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed after rising copper prices helped reverse some of the recent losses from a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched last week, while \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was held back by concerns of further meddling in markets.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> strengthened 0.6 percent to 12.1400 per dollar, hitting its strongest level since April of last year, helped by data that showed local factories were gaining momentum at the end of 2010 as U.S. demand picked up. [ID:nN11130858]\par \par \uc2 "It seems that industrial production continues to do well and domestic consumption is picking up," said Benito Berber, an economist at Nomura in New York.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was poised to post an over two-year high if it firms a bit past 12.13 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Berber said the peso could have some trouble breaking past option barriers around 12.10 per dollar. However, if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pierces that level, the peso could quickly firm past 12 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The forecasts that are calling for the peso to trade below 12 per dollar are likely to be reached in the first quarter," Berber said.\par \par \uc2 In the short term, other analysts said that too many investors may have piled into the Mexican peso trade, too quickly, leaving the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  open to profit-taking in the short term.\par \par \uc2 "The Mexican trade is pretty crowded," said Flavia Cattan-Naslausky, a strategist at RBS Securities in New York. "We need to take a breather here before we take another move."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  LOOMS\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real underperformed Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday as the threat of more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Brazilian market weighed on the real <BRBY>, which bid only 0.06 percent stronger at 1.685 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's finance minister, Guido Mantega, said Monday he was sure the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not strengthen further, adding that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  via so-called reverse swaps in the futures market would carry little financial risk. [ID:nN10282474]\par \par \uc2 If reverse swaps are used, the real could weaken to 1.75-1.77 per dollar, according to one New York-based head \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader.\par \par \uc2 The government has taken a number of measures to try to put the brakes on the real's recent gains, including a new reserve requirement on banks' short U.S. dollar positions.\par \par \uc2 "Mantega's threats went largely ignored by the market, though he is making it quite clear that policymakers will fight very hard against any further BRL appreciation," said Nick Chamie of RBC in a research note.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> firmed 0.6 percent to 496.50 per dollar, helped by higher prices for copper, the country's main export.\par \par \uc2 "The peso's performance here is mainly following what is going on abroad," said Rodrigo Sarria, a trader at Celfin Capital in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 "We have copper going up, so we should see the market here trying to test new levels. We could see corrections between 15 and 18 pesos in the next few days, which would be half of how much the peso fell following \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso slumped last week after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced a massive dollar-buying plan to curb its strength. For more, see: [ID:nN1124735]. (Additional reporting by Maria Jose Latorre in Santiago; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)(REPEAT)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|ABX|BNX|RNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110114e71b001ma\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
