\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  dip on Portugal,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2011\par 14:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Fears over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in futures market weigh on real\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real loses 0.5 pct, Mexican peso down 0.3 pct\par \par \uc2 * Chile's peso falls to 4-month low against dollar\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Froilan Romero\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/SANTIAGO, Jan 10 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened on Monday as fears over euro zone debt resurfaced, prompting an exodus from riskier assets worldwide.\par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  threw Portugal a temporary lifeline on Monday by buying up its bonds, traders said, as market and peer pressure mounted for Lisbon to seek an international bailout. [ID:nLDE7090U2]\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real also suffered from concerns that the government could make further efforts to control the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The authorization of the country's sovereign wealth fund to operate in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was finally completed on Monday while speculation about action in the futures market intensified.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> was bid 0.47 percent weaker at 1.692 reais per U.S. dollar on the local spot market in early trading.\par \par \uc2 "The expectation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could act in (the) derivatives (futures market) is reinforcing the global move, it's a mix of global moves and local noise," said Roberto Padovani, chief Brazil economist with WestLB bank in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> weakened to a four-month low, falling 0.54 percent to 500.2 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 A major financial crisis in Europe would not only deter investment in emerging markets, but also the global economy, reducing demand for Latin American exports.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> slipped 0.29 percent to 12.2700 per dollar in dawn trading in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Chizu Nomiyama)\par \par \uc2 hold MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110113e71a0013z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
