\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Weaker As Government  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Weighs On Market\b0\par\par\uc2 By Matthew Cowley   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 447 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2011\par 14:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real weakened against the dollar on Monday, as investors are shy about taking a position with the constant threat of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hanging over their heads.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the government authorized its wealth fund to buy dollars, coming on the back of last week's move by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rein in the size of Brazilian banks' bets against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 "On the back of the steps announced last week, the tendency is for the real to weaken today and probably for the whole week, and it could test BRL1.70 soon," said Marcos Trabold, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the BT Associados Corretora de Cambio brokerage in Sao Paulo. "The government managed to cut part of the bank's speculative position."\par \par \uc2 The government's wealth fund can now buy or sell dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  spot and futures markets along with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the treasury, according to the authorization published in the federal register. The measure formalized the government's intention, expressed at the end of 2010, to allow the wealth fund to act in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 It's the latest in a series of measures which the government has taken to prevent the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from gaining too much ground against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Markets are also likely to spend much of the week debating the outcome of next week's monetary policy meeting, at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to raise interest rates. Higher rates are part of the reason why Brazil has been so attractive to foreign portfolio investment, especially given the low rates in the U.S. and Europe.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, expectations for IPCA consumer inflation in 2011 again nudged higher, to 5.34%, up from 5.32% a week earlier and up from 5.21% four weeks ago. The outlook for 2012 was stable at 4.50%, in line with the government's target. Last year, inflation reached 5.91%, the highest level since 2004.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was firmer against most major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid concerns over European sovereign financing. At 1253 GMT the real was trading at BRL1.6916 per dollar, weaker than the previous close of BRL1.6825, according to \uc2 Telekurs\uc2  via Factset.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the real was slightly stronger against the Chinese yuan, according to \uc2 Telekurs\uc2 , trading at CNY3.91 per real, from the previous close of CNY3.93. China is Brazil's largest trading partner.\par \par \uc2 -By Matthew Cowley, Dow Jones Newswires; +55 11 3544 7082; matthew.cowley@dowjones.com [ 10-01-11 1302GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110110e71a0018o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
