\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  flat after jobs,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 484 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2011\par 14:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real flat, Mexican peso weakens 0.1 pct\par \par \uc2 * U.S. jobs data offer no direction to region's markets\par \par \uc2 * Chile's peso gets temporary lift from copper export data\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments, reaction to U.S. data, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Maria Jose Latorre\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Jan 7 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded little changed on Friday after a mixed U.S. employment report left investors unclear about the pace of the economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 Investors were also reluctant to push the Brazilian real or the Chilean peso higher after both countries moved aggressively this week to curb the recent rise in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> lingered around its previous close, trading flat at 1.686 per dollar on the local market.\par \par \uc2 In the latest attempt to curb the real's gains, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it will impose an unremunerated reserve requirement of 60 percent on U.S. dollar short positions when certain limits are exceeded.\par \par \uc2 "Brazil seems to be moving in the direction of countries such as Colombia, where banks cannot carry short (dollar) positions in the spot market," said analysts at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in a research note.\par \par \uc2 "Regardless of whether the latest measures prove effective or not, one thing is clear: regulatory uncertainty is rising, and investors are asking, 'What next'? " according to the note.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> weakened 0.09 percent to 12.2425 per dollar. Mexico's markets follow U.S. data closely because of the countries' strong trading links.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> seesawed in early trading and was later down 0.44 percent at 497.50 per dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had weakened in early trading but managed to pare losses after data showed the country's copper export revenue rose 43 percent in 2010. [ID:nSGO002116]\par \par \uc2 "At the beginning of the day, the peso was around 497 per dollar, and then the export data helped to bring the peso to the 495 level," said one trader in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 But the U.S. payrolls data sent the peso down to the levels it dipped to in early trading. [ID:nN06134458]\par \par \uc2 Investors were also looking to Chile's interest rate decision next week, which could affect the short-term performance of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Chilean analysts are evenly divided on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hold its benchmark interest rate or raise it by 25 basis points, according to a Reuters poll conducted on Friday. [ID:nSAG002684]\par \par \uc2 "Some analysts are calling for a pause in the rate tightening cycle this month, but we still expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue raising rates, quite possibly for a few more months yet," said Clyde Wardle, an analyst with \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in New York, in a research note.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Padraic Cassidy)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110110e717000tb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
