\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Chile's peso tumbles; Mexican peso gains on US\b0\par\par\uc2 556 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2011\par 14:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Chile's peso falls 1.2 pct on first day of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real dips 0.1 pct, Mexican peso gains 0.1 pct\par \par \uc2 * Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  outperforms region after U.S. data (Adds reaction to U.S. employment data, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Brad Haynes\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/SANTIAGO, Jan 5 (Reuters) - Chile's peso and Brazil's real weakened on Wednesday as commodity prices fell and investors fretted over meddling in the countries' markets.\par \par \uc2 But Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is not seen to be at risk from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , managed to edge back into positive territory after encouraging U.S. employment data.\par \par \uc2 Chile's market was still reeling from Monday's news that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will buy $50 million daily to curb the peso's rise -- a program that kicks off on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, investors in the Brazilian market were cautious after the government issued fresh warnings on Tuesday that it was ready to take tougher action if the real firms further.\par \par \uc2 The lower price of commodities, a key export and economic lifeline for the continent, also hit the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nL3E7C50FQ]\par \par \uc2 After suffering its biggest one-day loss in more than 25 years in the previous session, the Chilean peso <CLP=> weakened 1.2 percent to a two-month low of 493.3 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The effect of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be magnified as the price of Chile's main export copper slips from record highs, but analysts are not expecting another drop as dramatic as Tuesday's plunge.\par \par \uc2 "Yesterday we saw the announcement effect, but starting today we'll be seeing the impact of real purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said analyst Osvaldo Cruz with BCI in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 "With the dollar auction included, we see the exchange rate between 487 and 493 pesos per dollar today."\par \par \uc2 MANTEGA'S MANTRA\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> seesawed in early trading, later bid 0.12 percent weaker at 1.664 reais per U.S. dollar on the local spot market.\par \par \uc2 If the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to weaken it is likely to find strong technical support at 1.70 per dollar -- a psychologically important level in itself. At that point, the real will bump against its 50-day simple moving average (1.699), its 100-day simple moving average (1.7052) and then the 23.6 percent Fibonacci retracement level from the May-to-October rally (1.7072).\par \par \uc2 "Finance Minister Mantega keeps repeating his mantra that the government has tools to prevent excessive appreciation, including further measures to restrain capital flows," said Zeina Latif, chief Brazil economist at RBS in Sao Paulo, in a research note. "But the point is that there might be few options remaining without crossing over to more heterodox measures."\par \par \uc2 "We should expect more verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with (the real) below 1.65, but not meaningful \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures," she added.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> also weakened in early trading but reversed after better-than-expected data on private sector employment in the United States, the country's top trading partner. [ID:nN05266445]\par \par \uc2 The peso firmed 0.17 percent to 12.205 per dollar. (Additional reporting by Maria Jose Latorre in Santiago; Editing by Andrea Ricci)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110108e71500071\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
