\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Policy  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Remains A Risk - RBC\b0\par\par\uc2 1,220 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2011\par 21:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Robert Flint, 212-416-2216; \par robert.flint@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2053 GMT [Dow Jones] Finance Minister Mantega didn't reveal anything new in his latest comments, only reinforcing that Brazilian policymakers stand very committed to stop any further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation, especially beyond the 1.65 level, said RBC analysts. There is likely to be very little USD/BRL downside versus the current level, the analysts add. RBC says the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will remain under heavy government pressure to either delay or limit any new rate hikes. The analysts see a continued risk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and policy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (anjali.cordeiro@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3:36 (Dow Jones) It's enjoying good ratings and plenty of media buzz, but the Oprah Winfrey Network, or OWN, a joint-venture between Winfrey and Discovery Communications (DISCA), has frustrated some longtime fans of the daytime talk show host who have to upgrade their pay-TV subscription in order to access the channel. For instance, subscribers to Cablevision's (CVC) "Family Basic" plan, which costs $141.75 per month and includes around 200 channels, have to pay an extra $11.95 per month to access OWN. An OWN representative says about 85M cable households out of a total of over 100M have access to the channel. (nat.worden@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Call us at (212) 416-2184 or email paul.vigna@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Visit the Market Talk blog at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 2029 GMT [Dow Jones] Long-end Tsy futures settle mixed Tuesday as FOMC minutes indicate improving US picture, but no change to Fed's $600B plan to recharge economy by purchasing Treasurys. Mar 10-yr note futures settle 4+/32 higher at 120-10, putting anticipated cash yields below 3.375% level, according to Optima Investment Research. Mar classic bond futures fall 6/32 to close at 121-10, putting issues' yield above 4.375% by contract expiration. (jacob.bunge@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2027 GMT [Dow Jones] The EUR/USD is weaker after a string of U.S. economic news bolstered optimism about the U.S. recovery with eyes now on jobs data later in the week, says BNZ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist Mike Jones. "Overnight, the good news continued as November factory orders recorded an unexpected increase." The pair was last at 1.3306. He says the market will now be focused on Friday's non-farm payrolls U.S. employment report and Fed's testimony to the Senate as these might help "shape USD sentiment." He tips support at 1.3250 with resistance at 1.3420. (lucy.craymer@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2025 GMT [Dow Jones] Though things in US aren't improving fast enough to warrant any tweaks to QE2, investors take Fed's guarded view of improving growth scenario as improved odds on increase in benchmark rate early next year. Feb 2012 fed funds futures settle 2 BPs lower Tuesday, priced for 90% chance that Fed will lift rate to 0.5% at expected Jan 2012 meeting of the FOMC. May '12 fed funds futures pricing in 84% chance that the key rate will rise to 0.75% by contract expiration May 31 of that year. (jacob.bunge@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2021 GMT [Dow Jones] Traders unload Eurodollar futures as FOMC minutes offer guardedly positive read on US job growth and economic expansion. Front-month Mar contract flat on the day at 99.635, maintaining view of three-month US dollar Libor rising to 0.365% from current 0.30281%, but later-dated 2011 contracts see room for the rate to range higher as credit mkts improve. Dec Eurodollars settle 4.5 BPs lower at 99.225, seeing the Libor at 0.775% before the year's out, up from 0.73% seen at close of trade Monday. (jacob.bunge@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2021 GMT [Dow Jones] The two-speed recovery, in which large economies inch forward while smaller economies power ahead, will continue in 2011, says Jonathan Webb of Bache, a unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Prudential Financial\f28 \uc2 \f2 . That makes USD, EUR, GBP and JPY unsure bets, with each having "some serious problems and near-zero interest rates." Webb identifies Asia, Scandinavia and Latin America as places to seek returns in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as BRL, \f28 \uc2 \f2 NOK\f28 \uc2 \f2  and SEK.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (bradley.davis@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2017 GMT [Dow Jones] As confidence around emerging-market assets rise, the smaller, more illiquid frontier markets will likely benefit in 2011 from the general improvement in investor sentiment, said Mirae Asset analysts. "With so much interest in emerging markets and as inflows continue to lift emerging market indices higher, eventually there may be some room for some of this underperformance by frontier markets to unwind," Mirae analysts wrote in their EM 2011 Outlook. They pinpointed the Middle East, North Africa, and Gulf Cooperation Council regions as areas that can attract particular attention if oil prices should continue to rise and real estate markets stabilize. (cynthia.lin@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2000 GMT [Dow Jones] The Fed minutes suggest policymakers are not inclined to fight the markets when it comes to the recent increase in interst rates. Eric Green of \f28 \uc2 \f2 TD Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  notes FOMC members listed explanations why rates backed up so far, so fast. "Many of which are familiar to us," he writes "That is, year end positioning, stronger growth prospects, higher deficits and fiscal stimulus, and a market reassessing the ultimate size of QE." Importantly, the minutes have no indication that members are inclined to curtail the program. "The Fed will follow through with the $600 billion," Green concludes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (kathleen.madigan@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1949 GMT [Dow Jones] The euro is likely to weaken versus the dollar due to the sovereign debt problems and sluggish economic growth in the euro zone, says Stephen Peacher, chief investment officer at insurance giant Sun Life. However, the dollar is likely to weaken against many higher-yielding emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as stronger economic growth boosts some investors' appetites for riskier assets. Peacher says the Canadian dollar is likely to bounce around parity because the US dollar is likely to get some support should the pace of US economic growth this year trump that of Canada. In recent trade, the US dollar buys C$0.9990. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1946 GMT [Dow Jones] The US dollar continued to hover close to parity with the Canadian dollar, trading at CAD0.9994. Canadian companies were "aggressive" buyers of U.S. dollars last year, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 TD Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts Shaun Osborne and Jacqui Douglas in a research note. "We suspect that the USD-positive flows also reflect Canadians' desire to purchase other USD-denominated assets - real estate, vehicles as well as other investments - while the USD looks relatively `cheap,'" they wrote. USD/CAD continued to hover close to parity with the Canadian dollar, trading late afternoon at 0.9994.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (chana.schoenberger@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1943 GMT [Dow Jones] Insurance giant Sun Life says buying corporate bonds offers better value than Treasurys as the US growth outlook brightens. "I am not a huge fan of Treasurys," says Stephen Peacher, chief investment officer at Sun Life. He expects 10-year Treasury yield to rise toward 4% by the end of 2011. (min.zeng@dowjones.com) [ 01-04-11 1553ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110104e714000d1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
