\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Govt  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  'Dangerous' Game\b0\par\par\uc2 1,264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2011\par 14:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1302 GMT [Dow Jones] Brazil's real should gain against the dollar in the short-term, but is at risk due to the possibility of government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , says Andre Perfeito, an economist at Gradual Investimentos. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  essentially means "controlling (the market) on the basis of fear, and that can be a dangerous game," says Perfeito. When the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  buys dollars, it issues real, which pressure inflation unless they're absorbed through debt issuance, he says. Moreover, a weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  makes imports more expensive, which adds to inflation, he says. (matthew.cowley@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1251 GMT [Dow Jones]--The Greek/German 10-year spread climbs 10 bps Monday to reach fresh historic highs of 963 bps in moderate trade of EUR15M on the local HDAT and European bond trading platform. "It is an unpleasant start to the trading year because Greece has partially decoupled from its alignment with other euro-periphery sovereign credits where spreads are tightening early in the session," says a senior local bond analyst. "The widening can only be explained by an absence of sufficient willing buyers to absorb the mild selling pressure. But there is little conviction in the move because its not based on local catalysts, it is occurring on a day where London capital markets are closed, and low volumes are magnifying Greek spread movements," he adds. (nick.skrekas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1238 GMT [Dow Jones] Flows in the Canadian dollar held up to normal levels in full holiday conditions last week, according to \uc2 UBS\uc2 , while flows in USD fell to 61% of the 12-month average, EUR flows sank to 44%, and JPY fell to 61%. CHF flows held up reasonably well at 69%. "The Swiss franc continues to benefit from raw safe haven appeal, which has been accentuated due to Switzerland's excellent fiscal health. This offers a stark and favorable contrast to the situation in many other European economies. With 20% of Swiss exports bound for Germany, the CHF is also popular with those who wish to position for growth and see the franc as Europe's best vehicle for achieving this," bank says. (katie.martin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1235 GMT 0000[Dow Jones]--The Czech koruna will likely firm to 24.0 vs the euro by the end of this year from just above 25.0 Monday, and any potential brief koruna weakness is a buying opportunity, says Raiffeisenbank. Debt concerns in some euro-zone countries may temporarily boost risk aversion and weaken central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and so the koruna could temporarily weaken to 25.4 vs the euro, the note says. "We recommend using any short-term koruna weakening to hedge against mid- and long-term koruna appreciation," Raiffeisen says. EUR/CZK trades at 25.04. (sean.carney@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1208 GMT [Dow Jones] Poland's gross domestic product, or GDP, will expand at a 4.1% rate in '11, from +3.7% in '10, Investbank says. The bank forecasts the Monetary Policy Council, or MPC, will hike key interest rate by 25 basis points in March, followed by two more 25 bps hikes in 2Q and 4Q. Overall, Investbank forecasts the key interest rate at 4.25% at the end of 2011. (malgorzata.halaba@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1133 GMT [Dow Jones] Euro Overnight Index Average fixed higher at the close to the year Friday at 0.817% versus Thursday's 0.393%. Monday, the interbank overnight rate is trading lower, at 0.30%-0.40% vs 0.35%-0.70% Friday. Markets are calm and the availability of liquidity is good even after the turn of the year, a trader says. Banks parked EUR104.458 billion in the ECB's 0.25% overnight deposit facility, nearly a one-month high. Earlier Monday, the 3-month Euribor fixed at 1.001% vs 1.006% Friday. (benjamin.krieger@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1119 GMT [Dow Jones] The Swiss consumer price index is expected to fall 0.1% on the month in December, compared with a 0.2% rise in November, according to five economists polled by DJN. Year-on-year, the CPI is expected to rise 0.4% compared with a rise of 0.2% in November. The data is due Thursday, Jan. 6. (goran.mijuk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1056 GMT [Dow Jones] India government bonds are off lows as traders bet on a cut in size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's INR110 billion bond auction this week, says a dealer with primary dealership. The most-traded 8.08% 2022 bond is at 100.11 from 100.23 at Friday's close after falling as low as 99.99 intraday. "The traders are also betting that the 12-year paper (8.08% 2022) could be a part of the RBI's INR120 billion buyback of bonds this week," he says. The dealer tips the 2022 bond in a 100.00-100.15 range for the rest of the session. (nupur.acharya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1054 GMT [Dow Jones] Crude oil futures scale fresh 26-month highs ahead of the release of key U.S. manufacturing data; the market anticipates stronger ISM manufacturing data, with the key PMI figure expected to rise to 57.1 last month from 56.6 in November. The oil market's focus will remain on U.S. macro data for clues on the global economic recovery, especially Friday's closely watched jobs report, Jim Ritterbusch at Rittersbusch & Associates says; February Nymex is up 67 cents at $92.05/bbl on Globex. (gurdeep.singh@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1044 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/INR forward premia is higher on heavy paying interest by market participants, bracing for at least a 25bp rate hike expected from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  later this month, says a senior trader with a privately-run bank. One-year forward premia are at 2.5850 from 2.55 late Friday. Still, markets are relatively quiet in a post-New Year lull and will likely resume trading in full swing gradually in the week, he says. \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 's rate-setting meeting will be held on Jan. 25. The trader tips one-year forward premia in a 2.55-2.70 range from the week. (khushita.vasant@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1044 GMT [Dow Jones] Poland's December PMI at 56.3, and CPI estimate at 3.1% support expectations of a rate hike in January, says ING economist Rafal Benecki. Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Marek Belka, who recently said euro-zone jitters slow zloty strengthening and tilt risks toward tightening, appears to have growing power to influence other MPC members. Still, many economists say tightening won't start before March, after the MPC gets a new CPI projection. (marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1039 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/INR is flat in a sluggish session on the first trading day of the new year, says a dealer with a state-run bank. The pair is steady with late Friday trade at 44.71 after touching an intraday high of 44.77 in early trade. "The equity markets have closed in the green, which has capped the USD's gains. We will take overnight cues from the U.S. market and the euro for Tuesday's session," he says. He tips the pair in a 44.65-44.75 range in the rest of the session. The Sensex ended up 0.3%. (nupur.acharya@dowjones.com) [ 01-03-11 0802ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110103e7130005k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
