\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Mexico builds buffers against investment swings\b0\par\par\uc2 798 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2010\par 20:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 * Mexico sits still as Brazil frets over flows\par \par \uc2 * IMF cheaply insures against investor flight\par \par \uc2 * With weak growth, Mexico draws fewer investor eyes\par \par \uc2 By Jean Luis Arce and Patrick Rucker\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Dec 17 (Reuters) - As Mexico's regional peers noisily guard against the day when foreign investors will pack up and go home, policymakers here are taking a wait-and-see approach.\par \par \uc2 Suppressing the urge to cool white-hot markets with capital controls, Mexico is quietly putting buffers in place against the swings and roundabouts of investor sentiment by modestly soaking up dollars and tapping global reserves without the clamor and howl heard from its neighbors.\par \par \uc2 Mexico was rewarded for its forbearance this week when the International Monetary Fund topped up its safety-net credit line to about $73 billion and extended its life for two years.\par \par \uc2 "We can only keep this (program) for our platinum members who are really having the right policy," IMF chief Dominique Strauss-Kahn said. "Mexico is among them."\par \par \uc2 Combined with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the credit line gives Mexico access to roughly $185 billion to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from potential shocks, still short of the $280-plus billion that Brazil has socked away. Mexico's reserves are worth about 10 percent of overall economic output, compared to about 15 percent in Brazil.\par \par \uc2 The lower level of international reserves means Mexico is not burdened by having to offset extra liquidity created by dollar purchases the same way Brazil is.\par \par \uc2 Analysts applauded the credit line as a cheap insurance policy against investor flight.\par \par \uc2 "(This is) a low-cost precautionary move that will provide a cushion in the event that re-normalization of U.S. interest rates triggers a disruptive... capital flight shock," \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 ' Eduardo Suarez wrote in a client note.\par \par \uc2 While Brazil tries to stifle inflows with high costs and other Latin American peers step up \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls, Mexico's patient blend of soft talk and slow action should serve the country in the long-term.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso was battered during the financial crisis in part because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not have enough foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ballast, but now hard-cash reserves and the IMF lifeline should shield the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from a punishing loss in value if another crisis hits, said Roberto Melzi, economist with \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The market penalized Mexico more than Brazil during the crisis," he said. "One could argue that in the event of another shock, Mexico would not be so severely penalized."\par \par \uc2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 For a graphic on capital flows to Latam:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/qeg94q"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/qeg94q }}}\par \par \uc2 For graph of Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, Reuters Xtra users can\par \par \uc2 right-click on <aMXFCRES>\par \par \uc2 For graph of Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, right-click on\par \par \uc2 <aBRFCRES> ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 CASH BONANZA\par \par \uc2 Along with other emerging markets, Latin America has been flooded with foreign cash from investors looking for returns that can outpace yields in developed economies.\par \par \uc2 The cash bonanza will likely sour when Europe and the United States get back on their feet and begin to raise interest rates, attracting funds back to the developed world.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, emerging markets are trying to get the most out of the attention by locking in cheap funding and keeping a lid on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains that could damage exports, while limiting the potential damage from a sharp reverse of flows.\par \par \uc2 Local economies are each balancing those tensions in their fashion: Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is warning of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken its peso, while \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  has ramped up the tax on outsiders buying local bonds. For factbox, see [ID:nSGE69503F]\par \par \uc2 Mexico, by comparison, has been squirreling away dollars in a passive auction process since March and pushed reserves to record highs, a position now bolstered by the IMF credit line which was first extended in 2009, although never used.\par \par \uc2 IMF officials congratulated Mexico this week as they topped up the fund and said the credit line could be a model for pre-crisis financial help that discourages nations with strong finances from building a bloated dollar war-chest.\par \par \uc2 In late September, Brazil's finance minister rapped nations for spurring a damaging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war - driving down the value of their home \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to give exports a lift.\par \par \uc2 But IMF Western Hemisphere chief Nicolas Eyzaguirre has also warned of the dangers of a global 'reserve war' where healthy nations spur a race to build out-sized reserves, sapping energy from the rest of the economy and fanning global imbalances.\par \par \uc2 The IMF would prefer to act as the liquidity provider of last resort in case of capital flight, Eyzaguirre has said. (Additional reporting by Michael O'Boyle in Mexico and Samantha Pearson in Sao Paulo, Editing by Chizu Nomiyama)\par \par \uc2 MEXICO-ECONOMY/HEDGES (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|D|E|RBN|M|U  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101220e6ch0019c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
