\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  dip on Spanish debt threat\b0\par\par\uc2 580 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2010\par 13:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real and Chilean peso weaken 0.2 pct\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso weakens less than 0.1 pct after U.S. data\par \par \uc2 * Flows dwindle as 2010 draws to a close (Recasts after U.S. data, adds comments, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Maria Jose Latorre\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/SANTIAGO, Dec 15 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened on Wednesday after ratings agency \uc2 Moody's\uc2  threatened to downgrade Spanish debt, renewing euro zone fears and prompting investors to sell higher-risk assets.\par \par \uc2 A major financial fallout in Europe would not only deter investment in emerging markets but also hit global growth, reducing demand for Latin American exports. For details, see [ID:nLDE6BE0BP].\par \par \uc2 Strong U.S. economic data offered some support later on Wednesday but failed to reverse the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' earlier losses.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> weakened 0.21 percent to 473.7 per dollar as the price of copper, the country's main export, fell.\par \par \uc2 "The peso is depreciating slightly because the external backdrop is pretty bad. Most stock markets are down and the U.S. dollar is also recovering against the euro," said one trader in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> was bid 0.18 percent weaker at 1.696 reais per U.S. dollar on the local spot market, but trading just stronger than the closely watched 1.70 level.\par \par \uc2 Over recent months, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's authorities have stepped up their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts in the market when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has strengthened past 1.70 and threatened to break the 1.65 per-dollar level.\par \par \uc2 SPORADIC HOLIDAY FLOWS\par \par \uc2 But as investors do their last few trades of the year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may feel less need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively, said Tony Volpon, head of emerging markets research for the Americas at Nomura in New York.\par \par \uc2 "They're reacting more sporadically because the flows are more sporadic," he said. "They have a good idea of what's going in and out because a lot of people call the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and tell them beforehand."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has a tight grip over the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, called two auctions to buy U.S. dollars almost every day between Sept. 8 and Nov. 10 but has ditched the second auction in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 "They'll schedule their auctions to meet the flows," added Nomura's Volpon. "And this time of year, the flows are more balanced because there is profit remittance and a lot of people here in New York are spending money so they're buying a lot of dollars."\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> was only 0.03 percent weaker at 12.395 per dollar, supported by some strong economic data from the United States.\par \par \uc2 U.S. manufacturing activity in New York rebounded in December and the country's industrial output posted its biggest gain since July, separate data showed on Wednesday. [ID:nN15122981]\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso is more responsive to changes in the U.S. economic outlook due to the countries' strong trading links.\par \par \uc2 "The market didn't take the (U.S.) positive numbers well enough to build positions...you have two forces here, the dollar is gaining strength, so that puts a little bit of pressure on dollar bears," said Italo Lombardi, a Latin American economist and strategist with \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in New York. (Additional reporting by Jean Luis Arce in Mexico City; Editing by Andrea Ricci)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101218e6cf0007z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
