\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil rates dip, Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  firms on US data\b0\par\par\uc2 601 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 2010\par 14:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Investors pare \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate hike bets after retail data\par \par \uc2 * Chile invokes \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as peso hits 30-mo high\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real firms 0.35 pct, Mexico peso adds 0.13 pct (Adds comments, changes byline, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jose de Castro and Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, Dec 14 (Reuters) - Yields on Brazilian interest rate futures fell on Tuesday after weaker than expected retail sales prompted bets the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be under less pressure to raise borrowing costs.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian retail sales rose only 0.4 percent in October from the prior month, which pushed market players to rethink widely-held expectations that Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise its benchmark interest rate - called the Selic - early next year to cool inflation pressures. For details, see [ID:nN14196422]\par \par \uc2 "Now there is some doubt over if, in fact, the Selic will go up and, if it goes up, by how much." said Jason Vieira, an analyst at the Cruzeiro do Sul brokerage.\par \par \uc2 The yield on the interest rate contract due January 2012 <DIJF2>, one of the most heavily-traded of the session, fell 5 basis points to 11.85 percent.\par \par \uc2 A head trader at a bank in New York noted that the drop in rates on Tuesday showed the market is now pricing in a rate hike of only about 30 basis points at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's next meeting in January. Last week, the market had been betting on a 50-basis-point increase.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across Latin America firmed after surprisingly strong November U.S. retail sales boosted optimism about consumer spending in one of the region's top trading partners.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <BRBY> bid 0.35 percent stronger at 1.693 per dollar. Traders were buying up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the real pierced the key 1.70 level without without prompting additional \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures, traders said.\par \par \uc2 CHILE JAWBONES\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso surged to a 30-month high on the back of record prices for the country's main export, copper, and despite warnings from officials that they could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> firmed 0.44 percent to 472.70 per dollar even after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief said policymakers were continuing to evaluate the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the peso's gains. [ID:nN14274122]\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso initially firmed the U.S. retail sales data, which boosted the outlook for Mexican exports to its top trading partner.\par \par \uc2 But the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave up gains late in the session after the U.S. Federal Reserve showed no signs of curtailing its economic stimulus measures, raising the prospect of accelerating U.S. economic growth and also inflation.\par \par \uc2 The Fed's statement sparked steep losses in the price of U.S. bonds, driving up yields.\par \par \uc2 That pushed investors to dump riskier Mexican debt in favor of the rising yields on safer U.S. bonds, undermining the peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investors bought dollars to sink into U.S. government debt.\par \par \uc2 The yield on the government's 10-year peso bond <MX10YT=RR> jumped 13 basis points to bid at 7.17 percent.\par \par \uc2 "People are expecting a possible boom now in the U.S. economy, and with that pushing up returns on U.S. bonds, it is more attractive to be in Treasuries," said an analyst at a foreign bank in Mexico who does not have permission to speak to media. (Additional reporting by Samantha Pearson in Sao Paulo)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101217e6ce000up\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
