\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  give up gains; real sinks\b0\par\par\uc2 418 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 2010\par 14:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * U.S. data boosts dollar, hitting region's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real sinks 0.7 pct on outflows, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Higher copper price helps support Chilean peso\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Dec 10 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  surrendered most of their early gains on Friday after the U.S. trade deficit narrowed much more than expected in October, boosting the dollar worldwide. [ID:nN10198692]\par \par \uc2 The region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had all firmed earlier in the session following a rush of strong data from China, one of the region's top trading partners.\par \par \uc2 Chinese imports and exports soared in November while bank lending topped forecasts, suggesting the booming Chinese economy will continue to gobble up Latin American commodities such as Chilean copper and Brazilian soybeans.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> firmed to a fresh 30-month high in early trading but was later flat at 476 per dollar. The price of copper, the country's main export, pared gains as the greenback strengthened but remained in positive territory, helping the peso to outperform.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> also gave up most of its early gains to trade 0.13 percent stronger at 12.4600 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL'S REAL SUFFERS MOST\par \par \uc2 But the Brazilian real <BRBY> reversed early gains to bid 0.70 percent weaker at 1.719 reais per U.S. dollar on the local spot market, heading for a weekly decline of 2 percent.\par \par \uc2 Traders said companies were moving money out of the country as the year comes to a close.\par \par \uc2 "At the end of the year there are a lot of remittances abroad, they're very localized deals," said Andre Ferreira, director of the Futura brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 At these levels, investors are also particularly wary of attempts by the authorities to curb the real's recent rally.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCB) has recently started calling two auctions a day, instead of just one, to buy U.S. dollars. Finance Minister Guido Mantega this week also threatened to take further action to contain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise as exporters continue to struggle to sell their produce abroad.\par \par \uc2 "With the USDBRL now close to 1.71, the BCB resumed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  once during the day, reinforcing our thesis that BCB becomes more aggressive below 1.70," wrote analysts at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in a research note. "We do not like BRL in the near-term."\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101213e6ca000uh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
