\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Strengthens Early On Solid Growth Data\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2010\par 13:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real strengthened in early trading Thursday despite continued uncertainties abroad as investors showed an enthusiastic response to upbeat local third-quarter growth data.\par \par \uc2 The real opened at BRL1.688 to the dollar after ending at BRL1.693 to the dollar Wednesday on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's IBGE statistics institute Thursday reported the country posted 6.7% growth in the third quarter from the same period last year. The figure matched market expectations and maintained the economy on pace to post growth of more than 7% this year.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, not even Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision late Wednesday to hold the country's reference Selic rate unchanged was enough to discourage buying in Brazilian assets as investors seek out attractive returns in local markets.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's elevated local interest rates have served as a catalyst for incoming investment over recent months as local authorities struggle to put a ceiling on a continuously strengthening real.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained more than 30% against the dollar since early 2009, causing headaches for the country's exporters and a weakening of its trade balance.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, is expected to maintain its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday with customary dollar purchases.\par \par \uc2 The bank in recent months had stepped up its dollar purchase auctions to two daily as part of an effort to contain the strengthening of the real and build the country's foreign reserves.\par \par \uc2 As of Wednesday, Brazil's reserves stood at $286.6 billion.\par \par \uc2 -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; (5561) 3335-0832, gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 09-12-10 1236GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1836 5053 5076   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101209e6c90013j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
