\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Risks To Remain Strong\b0\par\par\uc2 1,133 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2010\par 18:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Robert Flint, 212-416-2216; \par robert.flint@dowjones.com \par  \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1706 GMT [Dow Jones] More Brazilian government measures in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to subdue a strengthening local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remain a distinct possibility as long as present local and global monetary conditions hold, says RBS economist Flavia Cattan-Naslausky. a sharp move of the towards BRL1.65 increases the risk of more aggressive measures, including "increased layers of IOF (Financial \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tax)," she says. "The deteriorating balance of risks supporting renewed rate hikes has widened the interest rate differentials against high yield EM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in favor of the real," she says. "High commodity prices also remain supportive." (Gerald.Jeffris@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1700 GMT [Dow Jones] Treasury prices tick up again after a brief bout of selling. Fresh buyers emerge attracted by yields while concern about euro-zone debt also boosts some demand. Bond prices are still off the best levels of the day as 30-yr sale looms at 1 p.m. EST. In recent trade, the benchmark 10-year note is 11/32 higher to yield 3.228%. The 30-year bond is 16/32 higher to yield 4.426%.\par \par \uc2 (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1659 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds are up Thursday as a surge in yields to their highest since April prompts some bargain hunting. Bunds followed Treasurys lower in recent sessions after a U.S. plan to extend Bush-era tax cuts boosted growth prospects and raised fears that Treasury supply may have to rise to cover the shortfall. However, Treasurys managed to recover overnight, aiding bunds and gilts as well. Bunds were also garnering support from widening yield spreads on Spanish and Portuguese government bonds. The weak tone for the periphery was also underpinned by a three-notch downgrade of Ireland by Fitch and comments from the Irish Labor party which says its members will oppose the EU/IMF bailout package when it is put to a vote next Wednesday. March bunds are up 0.56 at 124.95 and the 10-year bund is up at 96.16 to yield 2.947%. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1656 GMT [Dow Jones] Emerging market debt slightly tighter vs Treasurys, continuing the strength of the last couple days. Risk premium on \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2 's Emerging Markets Bond Index Global is 2 basis points tighter to 272 basis points over Treasurys. Index flat. Possible monetary tightening in China in coming days is one major issue in focus. China 2 basis points tighter to 116 basis points over Treasurys. Its index is also flat. (anjali.cordeiro@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1654 GMT [Dow Jones] Emerging market debt slightly tighter vs Treasurys, continuing the strength of the last couple days. Risk premium on \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2 's Emerging Markets Bond Index Global is 2 basis points tighter to 272 basis points over Treasurys. Index flat. Possible monetary tightening in China in coming days is one major issue in focus. China 2 basis points tighter to 116 basis points over Treasurys. Its index is also flat. (anjali.cordeiro@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1650 GMT [Dow Jones] The Financial System Review from the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  released Thu shows monetary policy remains a balancing act for Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says TD Economics. On the one hand, high household indebtedness could be exacerbated by prolonging stimulative interest rates, it says. "On the other hand, substantial uncertainty in global financial markets, a moderating domestic economy, and increasing short-term interest rate disparity vis-\u224\'00\'E0-vis the US are enough to give the Bank cause to stay on hold until mid-2011," TD says. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1645 GMT [Dow Jones] With unemployment high, the outlook for bonds backed by private student loans is negative, said Cynthia Ullrich of Fitch, speaking during a conference call on Thu. The credit quality of FFELP collateral, however, remains strong, based on support provided by guarantors and reinsurance provided by the US Dept of Education for at least 97% of principal and accrued interest for FFELP loans.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (anusha.shrivastava@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1638 GMT [Dow Jones] Short-term US rate futures prices turn lower again as the market goes back to pricing in higher yields. Quarterly 2012 through 2013 contracts recently down as much as 4 BP. January 2012 fed-funds futures see strong likelihood of 1st Fed tightening in Dec of next year. Jan '12 prices in 90% chance for FOMC to lift funds rate to 0.5% at its Dec '11 meeting, up from 84% chance Wed, 54% chance Tues, and only 20% chance Mon. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1633 GMT [Dow Jones] The outlook for credit card debt-backed bonds is stable for 2011, say Fitch analysts. "The employment situation will drive performance," said Cynthia Ullrich of Fitch, speaking during a conference call on Thurs. Chargeoff levels are stable but elevated, averaging about 10% through most of 2010, she pointed out.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (anusha.shrivastava@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1631 GMT [Dow Jones] Municipal bonds calmer Thursday after large selloff Wednesday that brought prices to lowest levels since mid-November. Prices generally unchanged but a basis point or two firmer beyond 2032. Ten-year at 3.00% and 30-year at 4.62%, according to Municipal Market Data's generic triple-A yield scale. Tone remains tentative as propects for extension of Build America Bond authorization beyond its scheduled Dec. 31 dim. Lipper mui mutual fund data also due out Thursday after having declined sharply the past few weeks. Some smaller new issues being priced as market awaits a $1.3 billion World Trade Center deal carrying very long maturities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (stan.rosenberg@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1624 GMT [Dow Jones] The Fed's buying jolts Treasury traders, fueling some selling in the bond market. Short-dated notes now erase gains to trade flat while 10-yr and 30-yr pare most gains before the 30-yr sale at 1 p.m. EST. "A lot of bonds were offered to the Fed and they only took a select group. Many guys were caught long and thought the Fed would take them out of their positions," says Michael Franzese, head of Treasury trading at Wunderlich Securities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1623 GMT [Dow Jones] The Fed buys $8.309 billion in Treasurys with maturities between November 2016 and November 2017, with the bulk of the buying on the notes due April 2017. The amount of buying is within the range of $7 bln to $9 bln the Fed intends to buy for this \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Dealers submit $33.126 billion in bids. It is part of the Fed's $600 bln QE2 plan launched in earlier November.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (min.zeng@dowjones.com) [ 12-09-10 1206ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101209e6c9000bz\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\